   359	13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
   360	14. **Fragment thirteen (S19):** "Force-adjacent. Teague. Partial. Bronze. Impulse along the line of the frame at contact: from the ground, through the man, out at the hand, and nothing to either side of the line. Needs a thing to push against — the barricade, the ground under the feet; nothing at a distance; nothing from the air. A body's length. The cost back along the same line, every time, at the place the line comes out. Engagement field: close; braced. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Thirteenth."
   361	(Notice typography follows the edition's convention for system text. The notices must read aloud as prose.)
