   454	## 13. Sequence locks — firsts and silences the expansion must not break
   455	
   456	New winter, Treswick and leg episodes must leave each of these intact:
   457	- **Lira asks nobody for anything** from Norhold until "Will you mend it." (266th).
   458	- **Cael lies still for no one but Oryn,** and she has read him three times (sack, table, marsh's edge) until Millrace. **Oryn does not read Cael** before Millrace's deep reading; she reads his ribs' surface at most.
   459	- **Seln teaches nobody anything** before "Draft nothing. Just look." (280th, to Vastin).
   460	- **Seln and Vastin exchange no words** before the 277th long-table doorway.
   461	- **No Iron Wall is shown** before the cut (279th). No Force is shown in Cael's presence before the meadow cart (298th).
   462	- **Teague's crew never drills under Vastin's wall** before the pass morning, when the doctrine is told to them once.
   463	- **The tall woman says nothing to any of the six** until her question at the pass. **The broad man says nothing to them** until "Aye" (305th). **The older healer never speaks to them.** **The young one's name is never written** (said once, by the broad man, in the stream-bed).
   464	- **"Noted" adoption:** Vastin's first is the 298th (the grade); Teague's first is the 303rd (the crest); Oryn's "Everybody says that now" comes on the 304th.
   465	- **Vastin** takes no order without walking it back before Millrace's "Stand there". He does not sit in front of the crew between the cut and the road's last post (281st).
   466	- **Cleon** is above ground with the crew only once (the yard fire). Otherwise he is at noon at his tavern, or on the stair. He takes no notice of Cael until he is told.
   467	- **Oryn's hands** never come off a person with nothing done before the young one (no deaths on her north circuit).
   468	- **The mule** goes north with Oryn on the 281st and returns at Millrace on the 298th. From the fork to Millrace the boxes are carried on backs (ruling 16).
   469	- **The square and the station steps:** Cael never sets foot on them. He never looks at the crown except at the count-of-one.
   470	- **Cleon's name** is first heard by Cael on the 280th. **Treswick and the Deepstacks** are first spoken aloud at the 268th table.
   471	- **Karis cannot read the index as a grade** until the 298th. The leaf is not readable on the page before the seventh day of Cleon's week.
   472	- **Vastin has not read the directive or objection** before the shale camp (305th).
   473	- **Cael reads pages the wrong way round** until somewhere on Treswick's stair, and no longer does by the 297th.
   474	- **The clerk** stays unnamed and "do not name" holds. He has not asked three things by the 291st.
