273:## AFTER MOVEMENT 2 — chapters 8–14, days 51–69 past the Line (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
275:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
276:- **The finding is earned and entered.** Stillhounds answer Path discharge; Karis's hypothesis (with its water clause) became a finding only after the ford, entered in the log in Cael's hand at her dictation. It leaves two things unaccounted: the hundred and ten yards, and dusk. Nothing more is known.
277:- **Deployment since the Line: ONE** — a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53. None before; none after. Shadow is unused by Cael and stays sealed. Seln's use of his OWN native Shadow Path under water at the ford is not Cael's deployment and stands (it tested the water clause).
279:- **"They stop inside, where the tiers are": "they" are HEALERS.** The protected unit's full three-speech form is on the page at the steading's gate (ch13). Lira's thought about ranks is her own inference on the road. No healer appears; "the nearest walks a route and she's not due" stands; **Lira's ankle is not mended in this book** and her run on day 65 is a chosen risk.
281:- **Teague is absent:** back on the 57th and out again, known only by Pike's report. No meeting.
282:- **Bodies:** Cael bitten through the calf ("the calf in elevens"); Karis's hand cannot hold a pencil; Lira's ankle splinted, then walking; Brom's shoulder in a sling. Exact states are in the author's state section below, as corrected after repair.
283:- **All new canon KEEP** (plan audit §6): the lip stones; "the third" as a man of the hold; the flint fire on the road lit on the strength of the finding, with the hold unchanged; the well's bad air; Pike pricing Brom's part at "a fifth of forty"; the closing bare tack.
286:### Review record
287:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial (pass; one register priority), cold read (three clarity items), source-distance (6 tracked passages, no dense scene), plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — twelve applied by the coordinator). Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows below when the recheck returns.
289:### New canon minted (author's list)
295:- **The finding (flag), as dictated by Karis and written in Cael's log:** the stillhound hunts Path discharge; it hears and sees a little, and uses both only to keep its place and to try a quiet body with its teeth; water masks it at both ends (a wading hound goes to where the declaration was when it left dry ground; a Path held under water for an hour and a quarter drew nothing at eleven feet); there is no leader, only whichever moves first; they learn. Not accounted for: 110 yards; dusk.
296:- **"Discharge"** is Karis's lecturer's word for what leaves a person when a Path is used; assessors call it presence and mark it; a station reads it off a plate.
299:- **Seln's Path under water (flag):** on day 53 he lifts his own Shadow for the first time since the crossroads fire, to the chin in the near pool, and lets it go before he rises. His knife: narrow, dull, a hand long. "The cut" is his trade's word for the man placed where the subject will run.
300:- **The hold's arrangements:** the bowman goes down as the hirer's witness and stands on the cut bank; the carter waits with the cart at the last bend; Seln's case stays in the loft between the second box and the third for that one evening.
301:- **Injuries, as fixed on the page:** Brom, left forearm, two furrows from wrist to mid-arm, to the bone, fourteen stitches; opened again at the wrist on day 59 (a hand put out to steady the cart in a wet rut), seen at the fire that night; stitches out on day 64; closed clean and re-wrapped on day 66. Lira, right ankle, the ligaments, bound flat to a barrel-stave; a stick from the bowman on day 56, left against the inn wall on day 64. Karis, two cuts across each palm; bound fists, then strips; a pencil on day 68. Cael, left calf, in at the outside and out at the inside; eleven strides, then twenty (day 62), then "a leg on level ground" and nine uphill (day 69).
303:- **The carter's map (flag):** east of Thornwater, two days of ticks out, the double line leaves its straight, goes round a patch of bare hide and comes back to its line, with nothing drawn inside the bend. Karis calls it "a quiet place on the hide"; that word draws the carter's wife's three sentences.
305:- **Lowmarch:** undirected eastbound mail stops at Pike's plank; he gives out each piece twice and reads letters at dusk to people who have no letters; a spike under the plank holds finished slips; he rewrites the whole wall on fresh sized sailcloth when the order changes; a crew entered as *the shingle pair* is thirteenth from day 60.
306:- **Teague:** back down the cold road on the 57th; read the struck slip twice and the five's line; took two holds' slips from the north end of the plank and went up the north water at next light. Not seen.
307:- **The well (flag):** at the south road's fork, half a day out on level ground; a dry-stone curb, a windlass; paid from the standing-money. It went sour at the thaw; a carter's boy was drawn up asleep. Foul air lay fifteen feet deep on the water at thirty feet. Pike's line: *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.*
310:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
311:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the steading's woman's last word is about HEALERS ("Healer would've had it straight in an hour." / "There isn't one." / "There's not. They stop inside, where the tiers are."), Lira says "There isn't one", and nobody asks the woman about ranks; the thought that ranks stop there too is Lira's own, said at the fire. Cael learns of the bite when his left foot drags and he sits down in the river (Seln sees it first; no blood in the water). The finding begins as a line of Cael's own, which Karis strikes and replaces by dictation. The day-57 log gives no "earned" figure; Thornwater's yard has no stride count; Hesk's letter is known by its fold. Owner flag 5 above is superseded by the coordinator's amendment. Word counts, metrics, line numbers and the protected-units table elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the repaired chapter 13 also carries the protected three-speech unit at lines 35–41.*
315:**Where everyone is.** All five at Lowmarch, sleeping in the meadow, with the three boxes in the loft over the ferryman's drum. Teague and his three are out on two holds' slips up the north water.
317:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53, in front of the hold's bowman). Shadow unused; it lifted at dusk through the wait at the ford and again on the walk down the bar and was refused. Ember offered a point in the hound's mouth over Karis and was refused. The Iron read stays shut. Left calf bitten through on day 53: a leg on level ground, nine strides uphill. He has not asked Seln for his report, has not answered Lira's question, has not answered Hesk's letter, and has stopped counting Lira's runs. He knows that he had a grandmother who crossed the Line once on a trade run; no name, no line of descent.
319:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. Right ankle: ligaments, never seen by a healer, bound eleven days; no stick since day 64; runs on the gravel bar from day 65; "it bends less, and later". No burst at the ford or since. She killed one hound with the long knife. Her question stands unanswered in Cael's log. She has been told at Thornwater's gate that a healer would have had the ankle straight in an hour, and that there is none; she asked for nothing.
321:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. He declared once at the ford, on purpose, for about three breaths, and dropped it with the hound's teeth shut on his arm; he drowned that hound with his shoulder and the current. Left forearm: closed clean on day 66, re-wrapped by his own choice, "shut, not sound". He has carried nothing since day 53. He keeps Pike's six words ("Same as anyone. What'd he do?") on a dead slip inside his shirt.
323:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. One point lit and put out at the ford; none since. Two pink lines across each palm; a pencil again on day 68. Holds: the hypothesis leaf; the finding (in Cael's log, by her dictation, and in the field archive in Lira's hand); a leaf headed *This side.*; the carter's map; and, in the middle box, the carter's wife's three sentences with *everybody knows* underlined twice. She has asked nobody what quiet ground is, Seln included.
325:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze (not said in public). Lifted his Path once, under water, on day 53; killed the seventh hound. Unmarked. Walked the south road to the well first, alone, and said nothing. Has said aloud that he keeps waiting to be asked for his report. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut**; it spent the evening of day 53 in Thornwater's loft.
327:**Objects and money.** Three boxes over the ferry drum. The reserve unopened. Board purse: **sixty-two marks earned** (18 + ford 40 + well 4); **fifty-two in hand** (one mark on flour and bacon on day 51; one to the hold for linen and thread; coppers unitemised). Hesk's satchel holds the log (with the finding and the seal entry), the old volume, the observation notebook, Pike's two lines on bark, and Hesk's letter. Cael's coat has lost its left sleeve. The ash stick is propping an old carter's shaft under the ash.
329:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Six lines** under the five names: the protected ford line (said on day 60) and *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.* (day 64). **Twelfth of thirteen; Teague eleven up.** The ford slip is with the finished slips, struck with one line through Teague's name and five strokes beneath, and Thornwater's mark at the foot. Fourteen slips on the plank on day 60; a bare tack set by the left-hand post on the evening of day 69 for a hold's slip expected from the north-west.
331:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. The hold's bowman saw one Wind burst and took it for a Path. The party now holds the stillhound finding in five sentences. **Quiet ground is three sentences from a carter's wife**; nobody has asked Pike or anyone. Thornwater knows the five as the crew that came up from its ford. The party knows from the hold that one healer walks a route and is not due, and that healers otherwise "stop inside, where the tiers are". Teague has read the struck slip and the line and said nothing; no meeting.
333:**Open threads.** Two hounds gone down the river, logged as open. Why a hundred and ten yards; why dusk. What quiet ground is, and what a road bends round two days east of Thornwater. Lira's question. Hesk's letter and the roof. What Teague will say when they have cost him something. A hold's slip, with a ford in it, due on the oak in the morning.
