516:- **Correct Ring geometry:** western line stone to floor centre is 220 yards as printed; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is at the eastern lip. Therefore den to the western objective line is about 233 yards, and den to the eastern perimeter is about 207 yards. Do not reintroduce M4's discarded 150-yard figure (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:43-45,165-169,199-201`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:64-66`). The cord is approximately 21.9 yards by the protected circumference/radius figures, but its length and Karis's stride remain unstated (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:191-209`).
518:- **Rubbings after fix 7:** eleven complete Ring sheets exist; the last is rolled in Karis's coat and the others are in the middle box (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:99,131-163,237`; `BOOK_MAP.md:35`).
519:- **Bodies at dusk:** Cael's ribs remain taped until day 99 and his calf remains bound, not mended; Lira's tibia is new and barred from running until about day 110, her ankle remains unmended/taped, and she has drawn her knife; Brom's wrist is sound; Karis is three parts full; Seln is unmarked; Oryn cannot read or mend inside (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:23-43,181-233`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:207-215,237`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169-179`).
520:- **Secret/action count:** Cael alone knows the Iron read, foot of Wind and floor read worked. Shadow is unused; deployment since the Line remains one, and the day-96 log deliberately has no deployment line (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:239-299`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:63-77,219-235`).
521:- **Live Arbiter result:** Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira and Oryn fail at the same step; Cael's Arbiter was already dark and remains described only that way. Oryn knows no fragment mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:189-229`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:181-233,283-297`).
522:- **Hounds are still sign only:** Seln reads eight or nine fresh outward tracks to the east and none back; M5 may make the packet's nine visible, but no M4 character has yet seen one (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:155-193`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:18,24`).
523:- **Exact party/object placement:** six at the den; Brom wears the middle box; Seln is on one knee; Oryn's mule is hobbled west of the line stone with two panniers, six borrowed blankets, the unused left boot and covered crossbow; two boxes remain in Thornwater, with the reserve sealed in the third (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:13-29`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-7,219-239`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:167,183`).
524:- **Site evidence:** no instruments were found on the floor or within forty yards; stake 31 is registry-stamped, about five years weathered and untouched; the eleven uprights carry unknown bands round their feet (no band on the lip) [corrected at M4 close]; Karis's chips match nothing (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:107-143,219-235`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:53-123`).
525:- **Maps and withheld memory:** Karis's calfskin has three circles, two marked *guess*; the registry sheet has seven dashed roads and the Fallow is the third. Seln has not yet supplied his map-memory inference; that remains M5's (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:109-149`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:54-56`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:25-26`).
527:- **Letters:** Ephram, Vell and Hesk remain unanswered in Hesk's satchel; Bracken is male and Vell's session remains unexplained (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:59-83`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:55-101`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169,189`).
528:- **Oryn's route choice:** she replaced four extra table days plus the added deep-reading day with this road, explicitly owing Thornwater's short bench on return; she has been round the Ring by the ruts thirty times but had never crossed (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:223-231`; `manuscript/chapter-26.md:195-215`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:249-253`).
531:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the seven audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Pike speaks unasked, to the open ledger); Seln's case carried on the page (Oxhollow's ford; the east gate; ch30's gear); four tracked passages restaged, the ch30 floor scene re-entered on the bands (Lira sees writing from the turf; the lip found when Brom's cord will not lie down; nine chips rejected and three families tried); ch28's survey proved once; two anchors; a cadence pass. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES** — three applied by the coordinator: **Teague's fence is the axe-head hold's longer fence on the east road, forty marks, HOLD** (the repair's paddock job removed), and **Cael's overrun on the 96th is ONE quarter of an hour** (the repair's three quarters and the torn tenth sheet removed). Ruled KEEP: the cut bands run round the FOOT of each of the eleven uprights, a hand above the floor; no band on the lip; eleven finished, numbered sheets. All four tracked passages RESOLVED, no new tracking. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 36 protected. 37742 words. No markers remain.
534:## AFTER MOVEMENT 5 — chapters 31–37, dusk of day 96 to day 100 past the Line (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
536:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
537:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTEEN.** One at the ford (day 53) and twelve in the Ring on the night of the 96th, each priced and billed in the night log: Iron read; Shadow (once, ten strides); Wind; Pressure; Ember (one point on the knife's tip); Blade (an edge on Lira's knife); Anchor (perception only — a deliberate release counts); Storm lanes one, two and three (ten / ten / twelve counts; the body read lost while the air is held); Wind a second time; Compression at contact, late. The two noon tests of the 96th are left out of the number, unexplained. All capability rules held.
538:- **Shadow has been used ONCE and remains sealed.** Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln had the sightline; Oryn was screened and saw him arrive, not come; the pack is no witness. Oryn cannot identify Seln as its source. Seln struck Cael's second reason for silence ("I shall not be a reason… I should sooner have her told what may be done to her than be used to keep her ignorant") WITHOUT offering to be known as the source: Movement 6 tells her sources by Path, not by person, and the seal serves again at the Stair.
539:- **The Ring:** nine hounds counted on the white; two dead by Brom's bolts (thirteen feet; six feet); seven away "north and south along the line's outside", direction unobserved. The crossbow was on the mule; Seln fetched it during the retreat round the floor and Brom spanned it by hand. Bolts: six, five in the sleeve from the 97th. Geometry as closed in Movement 4.
540:- **Inside the line** no companion Path was used: Oryn's hands had nothing ("Nothing in my hands"); cloth and knees. Nobody has theorized why the fragments answered. *Quieting* has still not been said. "Compact" has been said aloud once, by Seln. Nothing is known of where the file is, what it says or why; dating stops at "five years… maybe six". Seln's map memory (maps with holes) is open; he asked for the carter's map.
541:- **The tenth fragment — Tide-adjacent — was acquired on the 100th** in Oryn's long reading (minute twenty-one); the notice is exact; "More than one" is said. **Cael let it happen without telling her first, with the covenant written beforehand, and told her the minute it was over. The page treats it as a wrong he did knowingly**: all four companions named it for what it is, he agreed that refusing would be right, and he chose against it. Writing it first made it knowing, not permitted. Oryn does NOT yet know the mechanism: her own naming of what was done, her terms and its cost to him are Movement 6's first scene. Integration cost is not yet paid.
542:- **Bodies:** Lira — right ankle gone a third time; forearm bitten and held, mended by Oryn outside the line (one mending "the size of two"), arm in a sling, walking flat-footed on Oryn's order; tibia mended earlier. Karis — throat, mended. Brom — ONE hand, the pads of FOUR fingers cut by the string, mended, four dark lines; no string until the 100th. Cael — the calf opened again on a stone (bound, closing by itself, not mended); left forearm (Compression's bill); ribs whole on the 99th. Oryn spent "three in two days… that's a route".
543:- **Money:** 108 in hand, unchanged. **Names:** none minted. **Length:** about 35,800 at draft; the Ring's 10,858 words accepted as earned.
545:### Review record
546:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial, cold read, source-distance (10 tracked passages; one dense scene, ch34 scene 3; one of the ten is now a restored protected unit), plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — 21 applied by the coordinator, including the four protected units the author had left as markers). Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows when the recheck returns.
548:### New canon minted (author's list)
554:- **Oryn's crossbow (flag):** has an iron stirrup at its nose and is spanned with a hook, which was in the near-side pannier and was not fetched; drawn by hand it cuts the fingers. It "throws low, a hand" at thirteen feet. A leather sleeve on the stock held **six** bolts. No history of the bow is given; Oryn says only that she looked at it at noon and left it, "a healer's reason".
555:- **Bolts:** one left in the hound on the floor; one cut out of the hound at the stone; **five in the sleeve** from the 97th. Karis keeps the sleeve while Brom may draw nothing.
558:- **Injuries, as fixed on the page:** Lira, left forearm bitten through between wrist and elbow, held about thirty counts, never shaken; mended in an hour at the line; eight small pink marks; slung in a strip of Thornwater's blanket, the hand under the opposite collarbone. Right ankle over outward a third time; taped on the 97th; flat-footed, whole sole. Karis, throat pressed by her own fists under the jaws; knuckles skinned; no voice on the 96th–97th; a croak on the 98th; single rasped words on the 99th. Brom, a straight cut across the pads of four fingers of ONE hand [corrected at close: the protected unit gives one hand, four finger-pads]; mended at noon on the 97th; nothing drawn until the hundredth. Cael, left calf opened along the old seam on a stone in the rut; bound by Karis in a blanket strip that stayed on until Thornwater's yard on the 99th (never bound or mended by Oryn) [corrected at close]; counting eleven strides on the 97th, about forty by the evening of the 98th, none by noon of the 99th; a pale seam "four days, counting the one it went on". Left forearm struck in the second lock; dead to the elbow that night; back to the wrist on the 99th. Ribs: the tape off in the yard on the 99th. Seln: nothing. Oryn: spent to the bottom on the 96th; two mendings at noon on the 97th; none on the 98th or 99th.
559:- **Oryn's rule for the long reading:** unfed, at first light, the door shut; the patient on his back with his head at the stool; a surface count first "so that I'd know I hadn't dreamed it"; her left hand under the nape and her right flat on the breastbone; she talks, "to keep my place". She says twenty minutes beforehand, "near enough".
562:- **Seln's memory (flag):** as a junior he carried a tin with a lead tag from one room to another and counted, without reading, eight fair linen-backed sheets of the country east of the Line: a ruled stroke for the Line, dashed roads carried farther than on the printed sheet, and on some sheets a small round ruled with a compass, empty, with a road going about one; no sign for it in the table at the sheet's foot; one sheet with two. He took them for something guarded. No room, office, year or name is given, and he says that he cannot place the second round.
563:- **The charcoal ring:** drawn on Karis's thin paper to the carter's measure (three things traced from the hide: the first water, Thornwater's square, a tick to a day; the rest from memory with the paper off the skin). Laid back on the hide it lies on her pencilled ring, a little larger, with one middle. The two rings marked *guess* are not promoted.
564:- **The posting read as a question:** by Seln, as inference: a paper that sends a crew to fetch what is not there asks only what becomes of the crew; the broker's clerk is to send word west by the next boat.
565:- **Thornwater:** five on the bench under the back room's window on the 99th, one a man who cut his shin with a scythe "at the start of the harvest"; she reads all five and puts them off until after noon on the 100th. The back room: one window in the eastern wall with a shutter, a bench under it, a scrubbed plank on two trestles, a three-legged stool, a peg on a thong for a latch; her things on a strip of canvas along the sill (tape on its stick, flask, shears, linen, horn cup, bone needle). The bowman takes off his cap when Lira comes in slung.
566:- **Oryn's route:** "the top gate of my round's eleven days north of here", by the road, at the mule's pace. No lateness figure is given.
567:- **Karis's page:** a single leaf, two years in the making: a curve for how quickly each fragment came, a column for what each cost afterward, and three words at its head. She calls it a model.
568:- **Small things:** Karis's lantern holds "three fingers" of oil after the hour and "a finger" in the loft. Seln makes Brom's bread to dictation and it does not burn. One of Thornwater's six blankets is returned a hand narrower. Lira climbs the loft ladder with her right hand and both knees.
570:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
571:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: Brom's hurt is ONE hand, four finger-pads; Oryn's rule for it is "Nothing on the string for three days"; Seln strikes Cael's second reason without offering to be known to Oryn; Lira's arm was first bound with Brom's folded cuff and strips of Oryn's shirt, her linen being on the mule; Cael's calf stays in Karis's blanket strip from the 96th until the yard on the 99th and is never bound by Oryn; the hound that Cael throws is let go by and helped on its way, after the jaws are levered open with the hilt of Lira's knife; the second lock is struck from behind, and he goes down onto the left forearm. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the markers it lists are filled.*
575:**Where everyone is.** Cael on the plank table with Oryn's hands on him, the door shut. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln in or about the loft over the barn, with all three boxes and the covenant leaf in Hesk's book. The mule in Thornwater's yard. Five of the hold's people waiting until after noon.
577:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Ten confirmed fragments** from the twentieth minute: the tenth is Tide-adjacent, partial, Iron, self and contact, *Acquisition: directed. Engagement: clinical — non-hostile.* It has not been tried, and its cost has not begun. The uncounted anomaly is untouched and unmentioned in this movement. **Deployment since the Line: thirteen** (the ford; twelve in the Ring on the 96th), as his log has it; the noon tests of the 96th are noted in the log as left out. Shadow used **once**. Ribs whole, the tape off on the 99th. Calf closed; it stayed in Karis's blanket strip from the night of the 96th until Oryn undid the knot in the yard on the 99th. Left forearm bruised and working (he came down on it under the hound's weight in the second lock). He knows that refusing would have been right and that the leaf permitted nothing; he chose against it and means to answer for it. He has told Oryn two things: that what she saw on the hill was his doing, and, in the last minute, "I need to tell you what I am." He has told nobody why anything answered him inside, and has not told Lira since when he knew. Three letters still unanswered.
579:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left forearm bitten through on the 96th, mended at the line; slung, and under the order until first snow** (nothing held, struck or caught). **Right ankle over a third time, taped, not mended**; she walks on the whole sole. The new tibia was run on for twenty yards and held. She knows that he chose not to act on the floor and that he had known he could; she has said "Later." and is keeping it. Her long knife is blunt.
581:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. **One hand, four finger-pads** laid open on the string, mended at noon on the 97th (four dark lines); **nothing on the string for three days, until the hundredth**. The folded linen cuff that he kept inside his shirt went to pad Lira's arm at the rim. He shot twice and killed twice. He carried the middle box through the whole of the Ring. He has the bill; the bow is his to carry and Karis has had the sleeve.
583:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **Nine points and eight joins for a count of six at the line on the 96th**; about a tenth left that night; nothing since. Throat mended on the 97th; hoarse single words by the 99th. Holds: eleven Ring sheets, dry, not yet looked at; the box unopened; the carter's map with three rings (two still *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet; her leaf *Where / Entered as said / Blank. Stamped. Filed.*; the stub and the entry against herself of the 99th. The two torn leaves lay on the loft's boards. She has asked him nothing.
585:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He fetched the bow, opened the jaws, carried Karis to the stone and called "Back". He has said "Compact" aloud once. He has given what he remembers of eight sheets and has refused to guess the file; nobody knows what such a file holds. He has struck Cael's second reason himself ("I should sooner have her told what may be done to her than be used to keep her ignorant") **without offering to be known to Oryn as a source**; the seal stands. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
587:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. Three mendings on the crew in two days; none since. She has crossed the line eight times alone at dawn on the 98th, which only Cael saw. She has read him five times at the surface and once at depth, and has found movement, "more than one", and no banks. She felt something change in him in the twentieth minute; she has been told that he did it and that he must tell her what he is; **she does not know the mechanism**. Thornwater's bench is owed four days and is put off until after noon.
589:**Objects and money.** Board purse unchanged: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** The Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box; no instruments were found; the posting (five strokes) is in Hesk's book. The crossbow, with **five bolts**, is with the crew; its spanning hook is in the mule's near-side pannier. One bolt lies on the Ring's floor. Six blankets returned, one a hand narrow. The rope is still owed.
593:**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged: seven lines; tenth; Teague nine up. The Fallow line has not been said. The two HOLD slips are unresolved on the page.
595:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five. Oryn knows that he can do, inside a line, what no Path can; she saw Wind, a light, and heard an edge ring; she did not see the Shadow use and cannot attribute his arrival at Karis. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln saw it. All six know that the registry's iron stands on the line, that maps were drawn with a blank there, and that the posting was a question which their coming out has answered. Nobody knows where the file is, what it says, or why. Nobody has said why the fragments answer inside.
597:**Open threads.** The telling, on the table, owed that minute. What it cost her, if anything. A leaf in a loft to be fetched and read. *Later*, on Lira's side. Seven hounds. A report going west with six on it. An arm slung until the snow, and an ankle that nobody has mended. Eleven sheets not yet looked at. Two rings marked *guess*. The top gate of a round, eleven days north.
