   401	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. **One involuntary full burst on the 78th**, when the ledge went (her body travelled about twenty feet; the declaration and its crack crossed the gorge); a second refused, six yards short of shelter. **Right tibia broken on the 78th, set and mended on the 80th: straight, new, to walk within the week and not to be run on for a month.** **Right ankle never mended** ("That's a tape and a season. It'll set."); she asked once, from the mule's back, on the 82nd; she tapes it herself as Oryn taught her and says that she now knows where it is. Her right boot is under the mountain; she is barefoot on that side. She rode Oryn's mule from the shoulder to Oxhollow and has not said the word.
   402	
   403	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration; the Skin did not start under the cart at the eighth narrowing. **Left forearm opened at the wrist on the 78th (two boxes), mended on the 80th; in a linen cuff; a week from the middle of the 80th, to take what sits on it and nothing that hangs from it.** He carried the third box down the mountain on his back. He has the hedging bill and the older ash wedge.
   404	
   405	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **One declaration on the 78th: nine points and eight channels, no join longer than eight paces, held eight seconds. Empty since;** told to ask nothing of herself for a week from the 80th. She could not strike a flint on the 78th, wrote one line on the 82nd and held the purse on the 84th. Holds: the derived page (shale-backs), in her hand, with the ford finding beside it in Lira's; everything in the three boxes; the carter's map. Her word on the herd stays "derived": derived on the 75th and used on the 78th, and not tested, since the ledge went and the declaration followed in the same breath, which is two causes in an accident and not one cause in a test. She has met a primary source who keeps no book, and has asked her nothing she was not invited to.
   406	
   407	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. No Path lifted. Unmarked. He asked leave on the 73rd to go ahead each day and find the sleeping place, and left scratched pebbles for word; he found every one, noted the pale rock, crossed the live slide for water, walked the lip twice and marked forty-four stones, and went down for help on the 80th, coming back alone ahead of the healer. He lent Karis his coat from the 78th. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.** He gave reports unasked on the 72nd, the 75th, the 79th and the 80th, since each bore.
   408	
   409	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken". **Her sum (her window, the 92nd):** whole on the 99th by the rule, though her hands say sooner; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; her Thornwater stop ends on the 95th; she means to work four days more at Thornwater's table and has put one day on the route, for the reading. She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record. She told Teague on the hill only that she was late.
   410	
   411	**Teague.** At Oxhollow's ford at dusk on the 84th he said his four things and crossed. He knows: no cart; a wrist in a healer's cuff; the girl's foot strapped; the small one asleep sitting up; the boy's ribs taped; that the mountain came down and all five came off it, mostly on their feet; that the keeper paid seventy for a no. **He knows that the healer was late to the upper hold on the 81st, where he had waited a day for the bow's hip, and he does not know why; he has not connected it with the five.** He does not know what Cael is. He and his three (the spear, the bow, the boy) and two mules are a day ahead on the road south.
   412	
   413	**Objects and money.** **The cart is in the gorge**, with the ferryman's rope, the blankets, the kettle, the canvas and the flour. Three boxes, whole, and Brom's ash wedge beside them; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. Seln's case. Hesk's satchel, with the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and Pike's lines on bark. Karis's lantern, cord, brass straightedge and Hesk's clock. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two marks earned** (62 + Oxhollow 70); **a hundred and sixteen in hand**; **six owed to the smith** for the cart. Pike's slip is in hand, with five strokes and Oxhollow's mark at its foot, to be carried to the plank. The long leaf was unrolled on the keeper's board and paid for there; the text does not say who carries it away, and the keeper is its buyer.
   414	
   415	**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged since the 69th: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up. The traverse is not yet said.
   416	
   417	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. Oryn knows that a healer's hands cannot read him and that he heals fast; she has been told nothing. Oxhollow's keeper knows that a Path used under the shale-backs brings the hill down, as derived. **Nobody has mentioned quiet ground.** Oryn's other holds are unnamed; Thornwater and Oxhollow are the only two named.
   418	
   419	**Open threads.** A fourth reading, promised at Thornwater in nine days and not possible, by her own sum, before the hundredth; and what four of the five felt when a healer said "both hands, and all of me". Twenty-one days of tape. Karis's reserve. A leg that may not run for a month and an ankle that will set. Six marks owed for a cart, and a rope. What Pike will write for a job that delivered a no and lost a cart. "The same contract inside a season." Animals lost from a hill, heard and not sworn, and twenty-five counted. Two hounds still open below Thornwater's ford. Lira's question, now with a job in it and a ledge under it. Hesk's letter, and no roof.
