   615	### Coordinator rulings (binding)
   616	- **The telling (day 100).** Oryn named what was done to her in her own terms and set the condition — **self first, ask first, tell her** — as HERS. Cael did not argue his reasons; nothing on the page forgives him for confessing; no consent was supplied after the fact; the acquisition stands. Her answer to what she would have said at the door is withheld, from the reader too. She was told the mechanism as a RETELLING of what the five established in Book 6 (his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word; the Arbiter went dark), sources by Path and not by person except the three she has touched. **Seln is not identified to her as the source of Shadow-adjacent.**
