   372	25. **Oryn at Millrace (S18):** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." / "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." / "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind."
   373	26. **The rate (S19 log):** "Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend."
   374	27. **The contract (S17):** "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall." / Force: "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice."
