   376	### Tier B — earlier books' wording quoted here (binding from source)
   377	
   378	- Karis (B7 Ch20): "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (in Ch1's form; S5, S15 and S20 use "A measurement is a fact about a ruler. Not about the hand that held it.")
   379	- Karis (B7 Ch24): "Someone made this pattern." Karis (B7 Ch23): "Three points make a line. Four make an argument."
   380	- Oryn (B7 Ch23): "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." Oryn's letter (B7 Ch24): "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O." / "Six, by letter."
   381	- Hesk's straightedge note (B7 Ch24): "Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H."
   382	- Teague (B7 Ch24): "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." Pike (B7 Ch24): "I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small."
   383	- Vastin (B6): "I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be."
   384	- The still-place inventory (B7 Ch24): "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues." Oryn: "stop touching it". The Tide rule: "ask first, every time".
   385	- The kit's ledger: "third site confirmed on bearing". The audio rule: "the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories.
