editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:18:It is dawn on the 299th, at Millrace ford. There are twelve and a mule. Teague's wrist is wrapped. Vastin is on day 20. Karis is writing with the bound hand. Oryn's road runs east with them for a day and a half and then it does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:31:- **The crest.** The watch-post: hut, fire, kit under a hide, two timbers, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." Seln: "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" Cael draws it. "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / Teague's **first "Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:35:  3. The watch reforms. **"Nothing was gained inside" is entered first.** "By count." Five go over stake thirty-four (Cael, then Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin) and four stay on the shelf. They walk. The pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east one at a time and is not pursued.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:66:A notch in the hills to the east, low and square, where the bearing runs. Seln did not like it and will look again from nearer. Past it, by the office's distance, the oldest site waits. Cael wants it more than anything since he was fourteen, and he has told Karis why. He was right. He does not yet know how right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:41:- Vastin's age is not stated. The clerk is not named and asks nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:31:  - **Vastin learning to be nobody**, badly. He moves toward the lamp four times on the fourth day. "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:49:- Vastin does not know the mechanism and his age is not stated. "Forty years" is his rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:17:It is the 294th day. The list of parts takes all day, and Cleon's finger is on the last line at the bell. Twelve fragments. Karis's hand is bound and she writes with it anyway. Vastin is on day 15 of a month. There is still no mule.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **Dawn (299th).** Twelve and a mule. The pencil line runs from the fourth circle onto the blank sheet and past the divider's point.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:42:- The grade is observation only, with no who and no why. No first-tier site appears. "Four hundred years" occurs only in the fixed 298th log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:52:Twelve walk east along a straightedge's line, two of them on no wall's count. A healer's route and a researcher's archive ride on one mule. A boy carries two findings that do not agree and a warning that has started to lean. Five days out is a fence the Compact built, and somebody is still watching it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:11:  - The previous ending is this edition's `manuscript/chapter-53.md`.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:17:It is first light on the 306th, at the shale camp below the notch. Seln comes back wet to the ankle from the pass's floor. Twelve and a mule. Vastin is on day 27. The ribs have been quiet since the marsh, and the thirteenth is listening.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:26:  - **The tall woman speaks to the six** for the first time in a year: "And then?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:33:- **Burial and the plain's edge (306th).** Teague's crew builds the cairn in their own order. The six carry at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." **"That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now."** No term tonight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:34:- **The still place, read as made (~3,000).** He recalls the warning by heart. Then **the twelfth turned inward on purpose**: still; set; *bones*; *a floor with nothing built on it*; *an instruction with no language*. "The same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." He tells no one, not Lira, not Oryn, not Karis. The Arbiter is unchanged. **The instruments read wronger**: the cord a stride short, the edges a hair and a half to two out. The trend is up and he draws no line. **The log, verbatim** ("the whole year").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:51:- The death is brief and not graphic. Its cost carries: eleven, the gap where a fourth stood, and Teague one short and not saying the number. Nobody strikes a retreating opponent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:52:- Vastin does not ask and is not asked; there is no vote. Oryn has not heard the leaf. Cael is nineteen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:27:- **The spring (280th).** Three readers. The instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size; "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin has three reflexes: a directive, a classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. **Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael.** Cael does the sum: his Kindling day, five years and a hundred-some days back. He does not write it, and puts the sheet back. Then: "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone. **Close, verbatim:** Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:40:- Vastin's age is not stated. Oryn does not read Cael; "the one thing I'm walking up that road owing".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:17:It is the 291st day. After the alley the working party goes by the carts' street in daylight, with the boxes on a borrowed handcart. Karis's left hand is bound in a strip of Brom's shirt. Cael has eleven fragments and the eleventh has nothing to do. The clerk has not asked three things.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:28:- **The leaf (293rd morning).** Describe the object before the reading: horn-coloured, point-written, the scraped name with its first upright stroke. Karis reads it **aloud once** (§9; §10 Tier A 1), then paraphrases it once: "the Architect" is a title, about four hundred years ago, and the purpose is the un-bound. "Older. Made. Us." Cael catalogues the room, not himself. **The chronicle** is marked: "Marked." / "Marked." Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers with **two pages** and the ruler rule. The copy, with the gap drawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:32:**Cutaways (~4,500):** Vastin, ~2,000, alone after the leaf. "Aimed." His sentence stays stopped in his head too. **He does not join the leaf to the sigils, does no date arithmetic, and names no seals.** Oryn, ~2,500, at a hold on her route, where a fourteen-year-old's Kindling happens. She watches a child see a sigil nobody else can see, and thinks of a dark one. **She has not heard the leaf. Nobody dies.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:37:- **The reveal is spoken once.** "Four hundred years" appears only in the record's voice, in Karis's single paraphrase, and in Cael's pole-two sentence. "The Architect" is a title, never an agent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:41:- The light is deniable. Nothing hints at agency. Nineteen, and **no birthday**. "Eight days inside" is counted from the 284th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:17:It is the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line, the morning after the ferry's last run. Snow is on Lowmarch, the river is skinning with ice, and the ferryman is taking his ropes in. There are five at the lower inn. Lira's arm is slung and her ankle taped, by Oryn's order. Brom's shoulder is bound. Karis has fifty-two sheets, the kit and its ledger, and a map with four circles and a line through them. Seln has the case. Cael is nineteen, with ten fragments and a still place he does not touch. Hesk's straightedge is in his coat and there are 96 marks in hand. Teague's crew is across the yard at the upper inn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:40:- Cael is nineteen, with no birthday. He has ten fragments; the still place is not read or touched. **Oryn does not read Cael** (§13). Lira asks nobody for anything before Thornwater. **Seln teaches nobody.** The tall woman, the broad man and the older healer do not speak to the five. Teague's crew stays unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:53:Six at a table on the 270th, with the ice going next week and a map that runs east. Karis's answer lies west, inside walls, under a registry. Cael has spent five years staying out of registries. The kit reads everyone but him. He has written *west, and inside* and does not like the sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:30:  1. **The records.** A courier's flat holding six years of abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), and six rows. "More than four." The completion report is the last sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:43:- Vastin's **age is not stated** (OWNER #17; §12 C1). "Forty years" is his own rounding. The Compact's spans of time are anchored to events, not numbers (§12 C2).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:45:- **Nobody connects the date to anyone.** Seln's stillness goes unexplained, and Cael does not know what it was. "Six years" is the office's rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen (turned nineteen in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **No birthday this book.** Ribs quiet since the marsh, healed under a healer's two days that became four. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. The ten fragments are at rest. The still place is untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:20:| Vastin | Inside the Compact, writing nothing (one window in Book 7). **Age not stated in this edition** (OWNER #17). "Forty years" is his own rounding. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:41:**Karis knows:** the 52 sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall); that the carvings *command* rather than describe (from their shape, at the Hall); the strata; [UNBOUND] as a stratum limit (Book 7 Ch15, used once); the sub-layer; that the kit's index is an index, not what it indexes. She has read of the old scholars' provision in a register "years ago".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:32:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:33:- **The reveal is delivered once, in the record's voice:** the leaf in the Deepstacks. "The Architect" is the record's title; the name is scraped away; it was about four hundred years ago; the purpose was "that the un-bound should not come again". The chronicle's "went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" is **marked, not read**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:51:1. **KEEP — The winter frame (S1, 131st–264th).** The ferry has gone and the count has stopped moving. Inventory: nineteen, ten fragments, 96 marks. The winter is priced: "Meadow rate is four a month for a crew that's on my sheet" / "Eleventh", twenty paid in front, leaving 76. Teague's chin-lift across the yard; the season line left blank on purpose.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:60:10. **KEEP — The handover (277th evening)**, in Vastin's stated order. First, the records: a courier's flat of six years of survey abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), six rows, "More than four", and the completion report as the last sheet. Second, the page: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". Third, the technician's sheet: the deep-layer line and the brush bar; Karis copies it and writes "not read". Seln goes still and does not say the sum. Vastin's vertigo; Karis owns the response. Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:63:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (his Kindling day; five years and a hundred-some days; "six" is the office's rounding), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:71:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:81:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:83:33. **KEEP — The crest (303rd).** The watch-post: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, a two-timber barricade, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" "Nobody declares. Nobody dies … Noted?" / Teague's first **"Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:84:34. **KEEP — The Span (304th).** First exchange: the watch's declaration is unanswered; Brom takes bolts on Iron. Teague goes through the middle (the barricade a body's length back) → **Force acquired** at a stride. Recoil: wrist, then elbow. The watch reforms. **Width:** "Nothing was gained inside" is entered first. "By count": five over stake thirty-four (Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin), four on the shelf. They walk to the pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east, unpursued. The win sentence (§10). The broad man goes over the sink's edge in the fourth second; Teague does not turn. Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers' nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's bill. **The Span** at noon: an arch on two piers over the sink, carvings on the piers' inner faces, the bearing "Through". Nothing happens on the crown. The thirteenth listens. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall woman's first words to the six in a year.** The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:87:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:155:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:159:Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:174:| 8 | The Sunken Span | 47–53 | 35,000 | S19, S20 (+the leg) | The leg on the page; the watch, the width and the thirteenth; the lamps finding and the crack. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:194:| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:227:| 290 | The alley; **Karis's hand cut**; fragment eleven |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:228:| 291 | The reader; fragment twelve; the warning |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:237:| 299 | Dawn: twelve and a mule; the Stair's bowl |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:247:Running counts that must reconcile: **Lira's arm** "fifteen days" at 280, "twenty-five" at 290, "twenty-seven" at 292 and "thirty-three" at 298 (counting the 266th as day 1). **Karis's hand** is eight days old on the 298th. **Cash:** 96 → 76 → 116 → 118 → 138 → 136 → 130 → 127 → 123. **Oryn's route:** count "days past the end of her road" from the cairn on the 300th (§12 C3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:299:| Paragraph median | **51** | ~18 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:323:- **The Span (M8).** A shelf a cart's width wide, with the sink's three-man drop on the left and the iron on the right; the line lies a stride past the iron. A barricade of two timbers stands at the shelf's narrowest; past the fire is a pinch a stride and a half wide, then a perimeter road a pace wide. There are seven defenders: two crossbows and an empty-handed low practitioner. Exchange one belongs to the watch. Exchange two: Teague's line, with Cael at his left a stride back. Exchange three: width (five inside two strides in, four on the shelf; walk; eleven seconds). Then the fall. **Fairness is entered before the act:** nothing is gained inside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:332:- **"Four hundred years"** appears only in the record's voice (the leaf's head, given in Karis's single paraphrase) and at the fixed positions: Cael's pole-two sentence, the 298th log, the 305th close dialogue and the closing prose. Do not add uses.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:347:1. **The leaf (S15):** "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:358:12. **Fragment eleven (S12):** "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:359:13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:363:16. **The grade (S17):** "A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's *for*." … "The one on a sheet says how *old* the thing is." / "Somebody laid them down in order" / "It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means." / Teague: "Oldest last." … "Then that's where we're going."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:364:17. **Pole two (S16):** Lira: "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Cael: "For five years I thought the system forgot to make room for me," … "It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." … "I happened anyway." / Lira: "Yeah." … "Now what." / Cael: "Now we find out how old the oldest one is. Karis has a bearing and the marks, and the records to read them against. There's a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine." … "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:368:21. **The court (S23–24):** Vastin: "I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." / Karis: "It's the first one." / Lira: "Right." / Oryn: "Nothing," … "Everything, round it." … "Same as you." / Teague: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough." … "Field's mine. This isn't field." / at the centre: "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:381:- Hesk's straightedge note (B7 Ch24): "Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:382:- Teague (B7 Ch24): "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." Pike (B7 Ch24): "I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:389:- **Ch1 closing log (270th):** "The ferry runs when the ice goes. Karis has a bearing, an index she can't read, and a language she can't read, and she says the answers are in a border archive nobody's opened since before the Compact. I've spent five years staying out of registries because a registry is where they file you. She wants me to walk into the oldest one on the continent. The kit reads everyone but me. So does the world, mostly. Nineteen. Ice goes next week. West, and inside, for the first time since the academy above Ostrand — which is a sentence I did not think I'd write again." And the 168th: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:390:- **Thornwater:** "Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off." / "Will you mend it." / "Lie still" / "It's an arm. Use it. It'll be slow for a month and it'll ache in the wet for a year and then it won't. Don't fall on it." / "I don't know what that is." … "Neither do you. Write that down too."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:391:- **S2 doorway:** "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. **S2 close:** "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." … "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." Also: "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." / "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." / "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:392:- **S4 lesson and log:** "The wall held the line," … "And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." … "I have never once in forty years needed someone else to be the reason." / "You do now," / "I know fields. I don't know packs." … "I'll learn or I won't." Log: "Vastin fought. He rooted the road and nearly got eaten for it — a wall's no good if you're the only thing making noise behind it. He knows fields. He doesn't know packs. He'll learn or he won't. Watched an Iron Wall go up two feet from me. Filed it. Note the day: an Archmarshal took a wound out here and there was no one to report it to. He looked almost free. Almost."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:393:- **S5:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." … "Draft nothing. Just look." / "Two copies of one ignorance." Close: "Six years," Karis said. "They measured all of it. They graded it — the sites are ranked by something, and it's the same something in the kit, and I can't read either one." … "Everything I can't read points at the same place." / "Treswick," / "The archive under it. Cleon." / "Who's Cleon?" / "The only historical-Path practitioner registered west of the Line. If the language is anywhere, it's under his hands. A day and a half." … "And then I find out whether I've been right for five years or wrong for five years, and I don't know which I'm more afraid of."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:396:- **S8:** "Entered by count. That's the door." Close: "Last time we walked into a place like this," … "it took four years and a hearing to walk out." / "Last time we didn't know what we were looking for." / "Do we now?" / "A name and a reason," … "Older than the walls, under our feet, and nobody's read it because nobody's had a reason to look and a person who could read it in the same lifetime." … "That's us. That's the whole reason it's still buried. We're the first ones who are both." (On "four years" see §12 C2: this is the one place where Cael's spoken rounding stands.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:398:- **S10:** "Older than [UNBOUND]," / "I know that hand." / "Being believed — " … "It's the end of being able to be wrong." / "Give me a week." / "I'm sorry," / "Don't be sorry," Seln said. "Be nobody." Log: "Karis has been looking for this room her whole life. Cleon's been sitting in it for thirty years waiting for her. Vastin tried to open a door with his rank and nearly closed all of them — an Archmarshal's worth nothing here, which he's taking about as well as I took [SHATTERED]. Down here the stone's older than the Compact, so the Compact doesn't reach. First place inside walls I've ever stood where nobody can file me, and it's a hole under a city, and it's because everything down here is older than the machine that files. Karis says give her a week. I've got a box to carry and a promise to keep about a station upstairs. I can wait."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:399:- **S11 close:** "You've been reading the strata. Old, older, oldest — I know, I read your face, you've dated these past anything the Compact admits." … "Here's what the strata can't tell you. These aren't the ruins of something. This is the *documentation* of something. Somebody wrote these down so the thing could be *built the same way twice*." … "In thirty years I never had the stone to match the text. You walked in with three floors." … "I don't think you're going to like what you've found, Karis. I've had a piece of it for a decade and I've never once slept well since." Also: "You think Karis is right? That it's all built on something?" / "I think we're about to find out." / "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." / Seln: "I looked at it." / log: "Brom was offered the life. He picked up the box." / "Seln looked at it. Decided nothing."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:400:- **S12:** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered somewhere, since I'm not the one who keeps the ledger any more." / "It's entered," Log: "Eleventh. Iron Wall, from Vastin, in an alley, while he held a line for us with nothing behind him but the decision to. It's not Brom's — Brom gets harder, this holds. I've spent five years learning to give ground and disappear. Now I've got the opposite in me, from the man who spent forty years being the wall they put in front of people like me. He held it for us instead. I don't have a word for what that is. I wrote it down anyway."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:403:- **S17 log:** "Karis cracked the grade. The sites are ranked by age and the bearing runs oldest-last — somebody laid them out in order, and the order runs into the deep edge, toward the first one they ever made. Second-tier's the fourth site, the one the Compact fenced. Third-tier's out past it, on the line, quiet for centuries. Teague's crew came for spring like he said — ten of us now, and he's still better at this than I am, and the ledger still says so. Two crews, one bearing, and a straightedge my guardian sent me because my grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. Turns out she was right about the line. Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." Also: "Two words," … "Both of them ours." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:404:- **S19:** "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / "Noted," / "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times," / win sentence: "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." / Teague's arm: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that now," Log body: "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth. Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend. The Span's the fourth site and the Compact fenced it, years ago by the scale on the iron, and left men on it. They knew. They've always known. The bearing runs through it and keeps going, oldest-last, and the oldest one's out there in the deep edge, quiet since they built the machine. One more site. I've wanted to stand in the middle of it since Karis said *someone made this.* Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:405:- **S20 close:** "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." / "And it's on the line." / "It's the *end* of the line. Oldest-last. Everything before it was practice, or maintenance, or — I don't have the word. This is the one that's been quiet since before quiet had a name." … "You still want to stand in the middle of it." / "More than I've wanted anything since I was fourteen." / "Why." / "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." / He was right. He did not yet know how right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:407:- **S22 log body:** "Turned the Rune fragment on myself. Cleon said don't. The reading only ever told me the still place was nothing — no flow, no current, a hole where a man should have a middle. The Rune sense says it's not a hole. It says it's *built like something* — like one of those floors with nothing standing on it. Same shape to that fragment as the sites are to Cleon's. I'm not going to write what that might mean, because I don't know, and because the last time I wrote something true in this log a healer made me swear an oath about it. The instruments read wronger for me than they did at Lowmarch. The trend's climbing. My Arbiter's still dark—nothing in me to go quiet, same as always. Tomorrow, the oldest one. I've spent the whole year wanting to stand in the middle of it. I think part of me already knows what I'm going to feel. Nothing. I think I'm going to feel nothing, and I think that's going to be the loudest thing that's ever happened to me." ("the whole year", never "the whole book".)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:409:- **S24 ledger:** "Thirteen: Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. One anomaly, the still place, read by two instruments — the tenth, which says nothing, and the twelfth, which says a shape — and understood by neither. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made. That is as far as the instruments go and I am not going past them." / "Stood in the middle of the first one. Nothing. Entered." **The letter:** "Nineteen. Your grandmother's line was already drawn. I followed it to the end; both edges agreed. Tell Lira's family I said so. Mind the shape, you said. I'm minding it. — C." (§12 C11.) Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road," … "If there's road."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:410:- **Closing prose (S24):** "He had spent the whole year learning that the world was built to prevent him — four hundred years of tiers and registries and a machine that lit for everyone but him, all of it laid down so that what he was would never come again. And at the center of the first place they ever made, the oldest silence on the continent, the one built before there was a word for it, he had felt no exclusion and no prevention and no wall. He had felt at home. He did not have a word for that yet. But he knew, now, walking back out across a floor older than the system that had expelled him, that it was not an accident — that the place built to end him was the one place he fit — and that the difference between *the system was built to exclude me* and *the system was built to prevent me* had a third sentence past it, waiting, that he was not ready to write. Someone had made the pattern. He was, he was beginning to understand, the pattern. That was as far as he could say."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:418:| **The Fractured Path predates the classification system** (the Architect designed it; ~400 years; the purpose was the un-bound) | **8 — DELIVER** | Deliver once, in the leaf (M6), in the record's voice. Karis paraphrases it once. Name scraped; "the Architect" is a title. The narrative reports the record's rationale and **does not endorse it**. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:436:- **C1 — Vastin's age.** The source states "Fifty-three, or near it" (S2), "at fifty-one" (S7) and "fifty-three-year-old" (S10). The universe ledger records 53. OWNER-DECISIONS #8/#17 default: *age never stated; career "forty years"*. **Edition: no stated age.** "Forty years" is kept as his own rounding (ruling 20). *Owner ruling welcome; it does not block.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:437:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** "five years" since the Kindling is correct and stays. Spans tied to the academy, the cache or Seln are anchored to events ("since the academy above Ostrand", "since a hearing", "since Norhold") rather than numbered. The single exception is Cael's own spoken rounding in the fixed S8 line, kept verbatim and heard as his rounding. *Owner may prefer to rewrite that line too.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:441:- **C6 — Architecture residue.** The architecture's header, plant ledger and checkpoint still say Cael turns twenty in Ch14, the terminus is "the Still Court", and there is a "sixth" site. **Superseded** by rulings 12 and 13 and by the closed prose: nineteen throughout, "the court", the fifth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:445:- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:447:- **C12 — "Six years" against "five years and a hundred-some days".** This is a deliberate rounding motif (ruling 14): "six" is the office's and the marshal's rounding. **Not a conflict. Keep both.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:450:- **C15 — Rhythm (not canon).** The source runs a 21.3-word sentence mean, 19% of sentences at forty words or more, and a paragraph median of 51. The edition re-builds the sentences (§7.4), and Tier C wording stays verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:488:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three holds and "Spring. Bring the map."; Teague's "Next spring" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael nineteen until his autumn birthday (about the 467th day), staged in Book 9. Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**

