1164:### Sol plan audit — inheritance for Movement 9 (binding)
1166:#### Dates and procedure
1168:- **Day 201, Fifth-day:** Brom's panel at the second bell; the ruling at the hour after noon. The ruling finds the enrollment lawful and Halcenvane compliant, grants compelled re-evaluation within five weeks, invokes chapter fourteen upon a null result, and makes revocation effective at the close of the present academic year (`manuscript/chapter-51.md:127–157,161–205`).
1169:- **Night of day 201 into day 202:** the council opens after the tenth bell; midnight sounds while Brom fetches Ephram (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:259–269`). The five hands therefore rise on **day 202, Sixth-day** (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:319–343`).
1170:- **Day 202, fourth bell:** the last bout. Cael wins two touches to one; Ephram's right shoulder is put out and set (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:97–137`).
1174:#### Bodies
1176:- **Cael:** left forearm bound, five Blade lines wrist to elbow, nothing broken, expected plum-dark for a fortnight; right hip has paid ten bursts, four past the oak's six; right shoulder has paid six pushes at load, one past Norhold's five; two ten-count lanes; headache/slow bill behind the eyes; one spark. No flag. M9 must carry the bruise and road bill so Book 7 can enter with the bruise about a week from gone and no open injury (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:65–137,204–210,298–306`; B6 `BOOK_MAP.md:97–100`; B7 `BOOK_MAP.md:19`).
1178:- **Brom:** two red bars across the forearms; otherwise sound. **Lira, Karis, Seln:** unhurt. Karis's fingers remain permanently paler from the earlier ignition margin (`manuscript/chapter-50.md:49–115`; B6 `BOOK_MAP.md:97–100`).
1180:#### Fragment inventory and deployments
1182:- **Nine confirmed fragments:** Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor-adjacent, Blade-adjacent. Session nine's Tide-adjacent anomaly remains uncounted. This is exactly Book 7's entry: “Nine confirmed fragments + the Tide-adjacent anomaly” (B7 `BOOK_MAP.md:19`).
1184:- **Blade is not deployed:** Cael sees the yard's edges for one breath and puts the new fragment down (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:39–49`). Its first integration pull is the yard-gate lintel's lower edge, named and quieted (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:310–320`).
1185:- **Anchor is not used in the yard; Shadow stays sealed.** The public sees Wind to ten, the fighting-load push, two Storm lanes, the give, one spark, and the deep read. The managed band is over. Book 7 must still open with “Deployment since the Line: none” (B6 `BOOK_MAP.md:74–79,533–539`; `packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:15–17,27`).
1187:#### Who knows what
1189:- **The cache/falsification revelation remains at six:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin. It is not filed, published, or used. Vastin knows the cache but never the mechanism (`BOOK_MAP.md:84–90,629–640`; `manuscript/chapter-52.md:61–105`).
1190:- **The integration mechanism remains at five:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln. Seln's allowance remains “twice more”; M8 does not spend a telling. Ephram, Withrow, Bracken, Ilsev, Havel, Rooke, Gault, Jent, and the public do not know it (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:99–103`; `manuscript/chapter-52.md:35,327–329`).
1191:- **Ephram** knows that all five are leaving east past the Line before the close and that Cael held the band deliberately. He knows neither cache nor mechanism and is never told that a fragment was taken (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:279–317`; `manuscript/chapter-54.md:270–286`).
1192:- **Withrow** knows the clean door, the five-day practical deadline, that Cael and others are going, and that the stair meeting involved “more than a ruling.” She deliberately does not ask what, how many, or when (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:15–17,31–57,79–93`).
1193:- **Bracken** knows four enrollees will withdraw before the year closes and has prepared four forms. He knows Brom's finding and guidance note. He does not know the cache or mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:121–185`; `manuscript/chapter-54.md:326–330`).
1197:#### Envelope, findings, forms, and boxes
1199:- Brom's **day-45 Velmere envelope** remains on his table, seal up, unopened. Beside it are the district finding and guidance slip, folded and unsigned. Brom has neither signed nor refused (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:117–123`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:1027–1028`; B6 `BOOK_MAP.md:91–96`). M9 may leave both papers there.
1200:- **Karis's three numbered research boxes** remain roped on the records-hall deposit shelf. Brom has promised to carry all three; M9 already assigns three trips (`manuscript/chapter-47.md:185–205`; `manuscript/chapter-52.md:159–171`; `packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:24`).
