editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen (turned nineteen in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **No birthday this book.** Ribs quiet since the marsh, healed under a healer's two days that became four. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. The ten fragments are at rest. The still place is untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:98:- Teague's spring term.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:25:- **Teague's crew** winters at Lowmarch: four plus the healer of no Path. His term: "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:38:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say."). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:39:- **Teague** turns west with three practitioners and the healer of no Path. **The young one is dead**, buried under stone at the pass's east mouth. His name was said once by the broad man and is never written. Teague carries Cael's letter to Hesk. "Next spring. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:51:1. **KEEP — The winter frame (S1, 131st–264th).** The ferry has gone and the count has stopped moving. Inventory: nineteen, ten fragments, 96 marks. The winter is priced: "Meadow rate is four a month for a crew that's on my sheet" / "Eleventh", twenty paid in front, leaving 76. Teague's chin-lift across the yard; the season line left blank on purpose.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:52:2. **KEEP — Pike's winter board and the fence (140th).** Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:56:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her spring's first stops. Nobody asked her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:63:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (his Kindling day; five years and a hundred-some days; "six" is the office's rounding), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:81:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:83:33. **KEEP — The crest (303rd).** The watch-post: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, a two-timber barricade, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" "Nobody declares. Nobody dies … Noted?" / Teague's first **"Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall woman's first words to the six in a year.** The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:87:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:89:39. **KEEP — The centre (307th dusk).** 506 strides. Rune turned on the floor at a hundred strides gives the same reading. The eyes are paid. **No edge, no seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. The third sentence goes unsaid. Oryn reads him at the line ("May I?"): "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He told nobody. The count. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:96:Nothing below may change an end state, move a death, add an acquisition, or disclose a reserved truth early (§11). Every new episode must fit the sequence locks in §13. Word figures are planning estimates, not quotas.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:105:| **The pass** (rig; seven volleys; the death) | S21, ~3,800 | 5,500 | This is the book's costliest fight. The terrain causes two beats (the fall, the swept scree). The young one's death must be prepared and not gratuitous. Force's first use is paid in the ribs. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:106:| **NEW — The shale-back herd at the axe-head fence** (winter) | summarized as "we walked the fence" | 3,000 | A winter set piece needing no Path: a herd of armoured grazers sheltering on the fence line's slope must be moved without stampeding them ("lethal on a slope when herded wrong"). It teaches the Iron read on frozen ground, Lira benched by her sling, Seln's posts, and Brom reading a line. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:108:| **NEW — The silent yard** (winter learning bouts with Teague's crew) | absent | 3 bouts × ~1,500 = 4,500 | No Paths, steel and bodies only, in the frozen meadow. Cael loses to the tall woman's spear reach (she never speaks), then corrects. One-armed Lira coaches from the bench. The rival clock appears on the page. This must not touch the sequence locks in §13 (no wall drill; Seln teaches nobody). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:113:| **Lesser exchanges given their beats** | — | ~4,500 | The alley's aftermath; the Span's broad-man fall; the ridge recovery of the mule; the court's pacing as a physical task. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:117:1. **Cael's working inventory in winter** (≈6,000; first third). Through private practice in the ferryman's shed and the frozen meadow, the reader learns all ten fragments as costs and limits. Wind's burst and its locked landing beat. Pressure's narrow channel. The Iron read as "the workhorse". Compression's frame. Ember, never used. Shadow's idle draw and the seal's logic. Storm asleep. Anchor used both ways. Blade, short and sharp. Tide "ask first", which he cannot practise on anyone and does not read on himself (Oryn said stop). **Invent no new numeric ceilings.** Costs are qualitative unless canon gives a number.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:119:3. **Vastin learning the crew's doctrine and "to be nobody"** (≈5,000, distributed). Day one of the border road is a silent-movement drill: walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless meant to be loud. Then the cut's lesson, the spring's "Draft nothing", the yard door's "Be nobody", his week of moving toward the lamp and stopping (four times, then two), and the first order he takes and keeps (Millrace).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:127:- **The winter months (131st–264th)** (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The board in winter. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:128:- **The week before the ferry (270th–276th)** (≈4,000). Tents return to the meadow. Teague's crew prepares for spring. Oryn's first Lowmarch stop: patients at the plank, seen from the outside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:132:- **The leg (299th–303rd)** (≈9,000). The Stair's bowl rim, where Karis checks a number for an hour. The cairn: Oryn chooses east. The Hall's marsh, where Cael read himself twice in the autumn. Two dry camps. Two crews learning each other. The crest at dusk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:142:| **Karis** | To be right and believed, with a primary source | Learns the kit. Makes the case for west. Owns the response to Vastin's flat. Reads the leaf once and asks that nobody say it back. Keeps two pages at a spring, a hole and a fire. Sits with Vastin after the pass. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Teague** | To be at the front of the thing; to keep his people | Holds the spring term. Names the contract's terms. Goes through the middle. Does not turn when the broad man falls. Does not put his three across the court's line. Carries the letter. | 7 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:148:| **Pike** | An honest ledger | Prices the winter. Prices Vastin at nothing yet. Leaves the season line blank, then dates it. | 4 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:167:| 1 | The Count Stopped Moving | 1–6 | 30,000 | S1 (whole) | Put the winter on the page; teach the ten fragments, the kit and the anomaly hard; pay the Thornwater promise; end on six and west. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:179:**Quiet-movement statement:** Movement 4 is the book's one deliberately partial-quiet movement. Its tension is legal and bodily: a [SHATTERED] body enters a Compact city whose top holds a station. Its learning encounter is the reading inward (the instrument fails). Its physical load is labour: four hands, three tiers, two gates, a bad knee and a box. It may carry one small physical beat of the author's choosing, but it does not need a fight. Every other movement has at least one fight, set piece or learning bout.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Karis** | ≈7,500 (3) | M1: a winter night with the kit's index (her want; the cord reads wrong only for him, and she refuses a theory). M5: decipherment (board numerals; the first letters). M8: the night after the lamps finding (the refusal held in her own head). | The sheets; strata; the index (as unreadable until the 298th); the leaf (after the 293rd); the lamps finding. | The Rune finding (nobody knows it). The integration of Rune before Cael tells Lira. **Drawing the line**: her interior names that the sentence exists and refuses it. The deep-layer date as Cael's Kindling. The leaf's content before it is read aloud. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:195:| **Teague** | ≈7,000 (3) | M1: the upper inn in winter, watching the five; the young one asking to learn; the wrist. M7: deciding the contract's terms; the meadow. M8: the watch's hut after the Span, counting. | His crew; Force and its line; the contract; the board; that he does not read. | The integration mechanism, including any suspicion that the boy took his Force. **The young one's name.** Any reading or writing (he does not read). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:197:**No cutaway may disclose a reserved truth (§11) or any sequence lock (§13).** A cutaway may show a person's private want and an independent decision. It must not reveal a fact the plot later "discovers" in Cael's POV.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:201:## 6. Calendar spine (continuity; the author may move scenes within a day)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:206:| 133 | Winter priced (76) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:215:| 270–276 | Tents; Lira's return bout; Teague's spring |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:219:| 280 | The spring (records); the fork-stone at evening |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:233:| 295 | Bridge; spring |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:275:- The winter inventory and practice (fragment names, costs, the seal, "deployment notes").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- **The cut (M3).** A hundred strides of road cut to a cart's width, with scree on both sides and a frozen runnel a stride wide down the middle. A sink lies fifty metres below on the north side, iced and in shadow; there are eight hounds. Positions: Brom on stone at the south edge with a rock; Vastin a stride behind him; Lira on the south scree; Seln on the north scree, unseen; Cael twenty strides west, past the sink; Karis, Oryn and the mule at the east end. The decisions: the wall goes up and everything turns to the loudest thing; Brom and Lira work its south end silently; Cael bursts **away**, then goes still on the scree as the lock beat lands; the pack returns to the wall and breaks on it; the heap; the runnel. The opponent learns too: the den has learned the road. Costs to carry: Brom's foot; Vastin's knee (a month); Cael's burst bill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:323:- **The Span (M8).** A shelf a cart's width wide, with the sink's three-man drop on the left and the iron on the right; the line lies a stride past the iron. A barricade of two timbers stands at the shelf's narrowest; past the fire is a pinch a stride and a half wide, then a perimeter road a pace wide. There are seven defenders: two crossbows and an empty-handed low practitioner. Exchange one belongs to the watch. Exchange two: Teague's line, with Cael at his left a stride back. Exchange three: width (five inside two strides in, four on the shelf; walk; eleven seconds). Then the fall. **Fairness is entered before the act:** nothing is gained inside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:324:- **The pass (M9).** A dry defile a hundred strides long with a loose-stone stream-bed. The west wall is scree to a shelf two-thirds up, carrying two timber-braced stacks, one with a roped dead pine; the east wall is sheer. The wall is a lean-to slant, high edge at the west wall ahead, low edge at the mouth behind. There are seven numbered volleys: Brom's forearm (1); the wall up (2); the fall (4); the broad man (5); the young one (6); Seln over the lip (7). Cael's push takes the second stack along the shelf, not off it. Teague goes up the stair left-handed; the tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks along the ridge. **Win sentence:** Seln removed the team's ability to hold the high ground by climbing the slope its own rig had swept clean, and the wall bought him the climb.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:354:8. **The lamps finding (S20):** "They fail the way a hundred lamps fail when one wire's cut. Not the way a hundred souls fall silent."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:369:22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "Spring's over," / "Noted," / "Next spring." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month,"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:380:- Oryn (B7 Ch23): "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." Oryn's letter (B7 Ch24): "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O." / "Six, by letter."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:382:- Teague (B7 Ch24): "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." Pike (B7 Ch24): "I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:390:- **Thornwater:** "Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off." / "Will you mend it." / "Lie still" / "It's an arm. Use it. It'll be slow for a month and it'll ache in the wet for a year and then it won't. Don't fall on it." / "I don't know what that is." … "Neither do you. Write that down too."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:403:- **S17 log:** "Karis cracked the grade. The sites are ranked by age and the bearing runs oldest-last — somebody laid them out in order, and the order runs into the deep edge, toward the first one they ever made. Second-tier's the fourth site, the one the Compact fenced. Third-tier's out past it, on the line, quiet for centuries. Teague's crew came for spring like he said — ten of us now, and he's still better at this than I am, and the ledger still says so. Two crews, one bearing, and a straightedge my guardian sent me because my grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. Turns out she was right about the line. Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." Also: "Two words," … "Both of them ours." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:437:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** "five years" since the Kindling is correct and stays. Spans tied to the academy, the cache or Seln are anchored to events ("since the academy above Ostrand", "since a hearing", "since Norhold") rather than numbered. The single exception is Cael's own spoken rounding in the fixed S8 line, kept verbatim and heard as his rounding. *Owner may prefer to rewrite that line too.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:446:- **C11 — "Tell Lira's family I said so"** (S24 letter to Hesk, kept by the final review). The referent is unclear: no Book 8 scene sets up Hesk carrying word to Lira's family. **Kept verbatim as source-fixed; owner to confirm intent** (it may be a callback the edition's earlier books should plant).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:456:New winter, Treswick and leg episodes must leave each of these intact:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:488:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three holds and "Spring. Bring the map."; Teague's "Next spring" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael nineteen until his autumn birthday (about the 467th day), staged in Book 9. Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:17:It is first light on the 306th, at the shale camp below the notch. Seln comes back wet to the ankle from the pass's floor. Twelve and a mule. Vastin is on day 27. The ribs have been quiet since the marsh, and the thirteenth is listening.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:26:  - **The tall woman speaks to the six** for the first time in a year: "And then?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:34:- **The still place, read as made (~3,000).** He recalls the warning by heart. Then **the twelfth turned inward on purpose**: still; set; *bones*; *a floor with nothing built on it*; *an instruction with no language*. "The same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." He tells no one, not Lira, not Oryn, not Karis. The Arbiter is unchanged. **The instruments read wronger**: the cord a stride short, the edges a hair and a half to two out. The trend is up and he draws no line. **The log, verbatim** ("the whole year").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:38:- **The line again.** Oryn: "May I?" / "Yes." "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He tells nobody what the centre felt like and gives them the count instead. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:39:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "Next spring … My crew comes." Oryn: "The day I have to." … "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say." "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:52:- Vastin does not ask and is not asked; there is no vote. Oryn has not heard the leaf. Cael is nineteen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:53:- Count Oryn's days past her road from the cairn (§12 C3). The letter's "Tell Lira's family I said so" stays verbatim (§12 C11).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:17:It is the morning of the 278th day. A new slip is pinned on Pike's plank: *Clearance. The cut below the shoulder hold, on the border road, two days west.* It pays twenty. Nobody has said Treswick aloud since the page. Vastin sits at the door end and is not on the sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:25:- **Road day one (278th, ~2,000):** a silent-movement drill for the newcomer. Walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless they are meant to be loud. Vastin walks at the back of the column, where a man walks who has not been told where to walk. He is learning the doctrine, not drilling under a wall (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:26:- **The cut (279th, ~3,500–4,000, developed).** Scout it from the lip first. The factor: "Carters declare, on the ice." Positions as in BOOK_MAP §8. **Iron Wall first shown:** a plane across the road, wall to wall. It holds eight hounds at a run, but the man holding it is rooted and becomes the loudest thing in the cut. Brom works its south end silent with a rock. Lira works the scree with two arms. Cael bursts *away*, then goes still on the scree while the lock beat lands. The pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap; Seln in the heap; the runnel; steel. Five dead and three into the sink ("clear because it's empty, not because it's safe"). Costs: Brom's foot. **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson, verbatim, and the log, verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:27:- **The spring (280th).** Three readers. The instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size; "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin has three reflexes: a directive, a classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. **Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael.** Cael does the sum: his Kindling day, five years and a hundred-some days back. He does not write it, and puts the sheet back. Then: "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone. **Close, verbatim:** Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:40:- Vastin's age is not stated. Oryn does not read Cael; "the one thing I'm walking up that road owing".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:17:It is the 294th day. The list of parts takes all day, and Cleon's finger is on the last line at the bell. Twelve fragments. Karis's hand is bound and she writes with it anyway. Vastin is on day 15 of a month. There is still no mule.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **Lowmarch (297th).** Pike: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.* The price and outcome columns are left blank, and the season line is dated. Cael reads the line the right way up. **Teague's term and contract, verbatim:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's. "Contract. Not more than that." / "The wall's still the wall." Cael prices it honestly: Teague is the better field captain, and the rival clock still runs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **Dawn (299th).** Twelve and a mule. The pencil line runs from the fourth circle onto the blank sheet and past the divider's point.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:42:- The grade is observation only, with no who and no why. No first-tier site appears. "Four hundred years" occurs only in the fixed 298th log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:52:Twelve walk east along a straightedge's line, two of them on no wall's count. A healer's route and a researcher's archive ride on one mule. A boy carries two findings that do not agree and a warning that has started to lean. Five days out is a fence the Compact built, and somebody is still watching it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:18:It is dawn on the 299th, at Millrace ford. There are twelve and a mule. Teague's wrist is wrapped. Vastin is on day 20. Karis is writing with the bound hand. Oryn's road runs east with them for a day and a half and then it does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:31:- **The crest.** The watch-post: hut, fire, kit under a hide, two timbers, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." Seln: "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" Cael draws it. "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / Teague's **first "Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:35:  3. The watch reforms. **"Nothing was gained inside" is entered first.** "By count." Five go over stake thirty-four (Cael, then Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin) and four stay on the shelf. They walk. The pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east one at a time and is not pursued.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:57:- The cairn is on the 300th. Count Oryn's days from it (§12 C3). No cutaway at the court.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:17:It is the 281st day, on the border road's last stretch. The city grows by the wayposts: nine miles, six, three. There are six of them and no mule. The boxes are on Brom's good shoulder, on Lira and on Cael, and the kit's case is on Vastin, who picked it up at the fork-stone unasked. Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:21:This is the book's one partly quiet movement. The reason: its tension is legal and bodily, a [SHATTERED] body entering a Compact city whose top holds a station. It does not need a fight. It holds a learning encounter in which an instrument fails, a confession, the city shown as a machine, and the irony that the only legal door into the oldest record of what Cael is admits him as a number. Progression teaching stays dense in the first third: the ten as currents, the Path-tiered city (passes, tier gates, the smith's two forges), and the provision's columns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:- **The reading inward (281st, the six-mile post).** First he works out the line between "stop touching it" and "do not read yourself". Then come the fourth and fifth readings. The ten are named as currents. The still place is read *around*, not touched. **Finding: the reading feels current; the still place has none; "a cord on a stone."** He needs an instrument for what does not move. He writes down later that he is afraid of that.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:41:- Vastin's age is not stated. The clerk is not named and asks nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:17:It is the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line, the morning after the ferry's last run. Snow is on Lowmarch, the river is skinning with ice, and the ferryman is taking his ropes in. There are five at the lower inn. Lira's arm is slung and her ankle taped, by Oryn's order. Brom's shoulder is bound. Karis has fifty-two sheets, the kit and its ledger, and a map with four circles and a line through them. Seln has the case. Cael is nineteen, with ten fragments and a still place he does not touch. Hesk's straightedge is in his coat and there are 96 marks in hand. Teague's crew is across the yard at the upper inn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:21:Put the winter on the page and teach hard. This is the first third, so the formula wants progression vocabulary at its densest here. The reader should finish the movement knowing all ten fragments as costs and limits, and the kit as a tool. They should know that instruments read wrong in one pair of hands, and why Karis cannot let go of the index. The movement ends with six at a table and a word nobody has said yet: west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:24:- **The winter priced** (133rd): Pike's four a month; "Eleventh"; seventy-six left. Then the board in winter: a roof, a well-house, a fence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:25:- **The fence at the axe-head hold** (~140th, ~3,000 for the set piece). This is two days out on the winter road. A shale-back herd shelters on the fence line's slope and must be moved without stampeding, with no Path that matters. Lira is benched in her sling and reads the herd for them. Brom reads the line of posts like a wall. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. The factor pays forty at the gate and asks no name: 116, and the tenth line, PAID.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:28:- **Cael's working inventory** (~6,000, across private practice in the ferryman's shed or the meadow at night). Each of the ten has its cost: Wind's burst and the lock beat; Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" when spoken); the Iron read; Compression's frame; Ember, unused; Shadow's idle draw and the seal; Storm asleep; Anchor used both ways; Blade; Tide, "ask first", which he does not run on himself.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:29:- **The anomaly as a scene** (168th). Karis has everyone pace the yard with the cord. It reads forty-two for everyone and "forty-one and a piece" for him, three times. The edges read a hair short and a hair long in his hands. Her ruler sentence is said twice, first as a rule and then not as one. Log it verbatim: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:31:- **Thornwater** (265th–266th). The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. "Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off." Oryn waits for Lira to undo the sling herself. "Will you mend it." / "Lie still": this is Lira's first ask since Norhold. The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole." The map on her table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "Neither do you. Write that down too." She will not read him yet. She comes down to Lowmarch, unasked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:40:- Cael is nineteen, with no birthday. He has ten fragments; the still place is not read or touched. **Oryn does not read Cael** (§13). Lira asks nobody for anything before Thornwater. **Seln teaches nobody.** The tall woman, the broad man and the older healer do not speak to the five. Teague's crew stays unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:53:Six at a table on the 270th, with the ice going next week and a map that runs east. Karis's answer lies west, inside walls, under a registry. Cael has spent five years staying out of registries. The kit reads everyone but him. He has written *west, and inside* and does not like the sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:17:It is the 291st day. After the alley the working party goes by the carts' street in daylight, with the boxes on a borrowed handcart. Karis's left hand is bound in a strip of Brom's shirt. Cael has eleven fragments and the eleventh has nothing to do. The clerk has not asked three things.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **Rune practice (~2,000, folded across the days).** The twelfth leans at every made thing: the inn table's joints, the bridge's arches, the dividers' hinge. He learns not to look, as he learned not to look at the light. It is never used on a person.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:28:- **The leaf (293rd morning).** Describe the object before the reading: horn-coloured, point-written, the scraped name with its first upright stroke. Karis reads it **aloud once** (§9; §10 Tier A 1), then paraphrases it once: "the Architect" is a title, about four hundred years ago, and the purpose is the un-bound. "Older. Made. Us." Cael catalogues the room, not himself. **The chronicle** is marked: "Marked." / "Marked." Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers with **two pages** and the ruler rule. The copy, with the gap drawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:32:**Cutaways (~4,500):** Vastin, ~2,000, alone after the leaf. "Aimed." His sentence stays stopped in his head too. **He does not join the leaf to the sigils, does no date arithmetic, and names no seals.** Oryn, ~2,500, at a hold on her route, where a fourteen-year-old's Kindling happens. She watches a child see a sigil nobody else can see, and thinks of a dark one. **She has not heard the leaf. Nobody dies.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:37:- **The reveal is spoken once.** "Four hundred years" appears only in the record's voice, in Karis's single paraphrase, and in Cael's pole-two sentence. "The Architect" is a title, never an agent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:41:- The light is deniable. Nothing hints at agency. Nineteen, and **no birthday**. "Eight days inside" is counted from the 284th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:17:It is the 284th day, under Treswick. The lamp goes into the middle gallery. A light is already on at its end, and a man is already reading.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:26:- **The chamber days (285th–289th; ~8,000 on the page, including the 288th–289th the source left undramatized).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:31:  - **Vastin learning to be nobody**, badly. He moves toward the lamp four times on the fourth day. "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:49:- Vastin does not know the mechanism and his age is not stated. "Forty years" is his rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:53:The galleries' geography. The order of the chamber days, and which small discoveries Karis makes on which day. Brom's yard and the broker's words. How the alley's minute feels from two feet below a plane. Where the humour sits: the lamp, the chairs with and without cushions, Brom's "Cart was heavier".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:57:The faction knows where they sleep, and they know the crew knows it. A man who held a wall for them has asked for it to be entered, and Cael has entered more than the man knows. Karis has three days left of Cleon's week. A board leans, and a boy holding a lamp has started to notice which way.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:17:It is the 270th day at Lowmarch. There are six now, with Oryn's spring stop at Pike's plank. Lira has two arms she does not quite trust, and Brom's shoulder is still bound and unread. The ferryman says the ice will go in a week, and has said so for a week. Karis's case is made and no one has answered it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:26:- **The ferry** (277th, first light). The river is in flood and the rope is strained, and a passenger holds a line physically, with no Path, before Cael knows the stance (~1,500). Then: "Cael knew the stance before he knew the face." "Vastin," Seln says, in the voice for an inventory. "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:30:  1. **The records.** A courier's flat holding six years of abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), and six rows. "More than four." The completion report is the last sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:43:- Vastin's **age is not stated** (OWNER #17; §12 C1). "Forty years" is his own rounding. The Compact's spans of time are anchored to events, not numbers (§12 C2).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:45:- **Nobody connects the date to anyone.** Seln's stillness goes unexplained, and Cael does not know what it was. "Six years" is the office's rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:7:## ENTRY — Movement 1, chapter 1 (Lowmarch; the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line; first snow, the day after the ferry's last run)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen (turned nineteen in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **No birthday this book.** Ribs quiet since the marsh, healed under a healer's two days that became four. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. The ten fragments are at rest. The still place is untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:19:| Teague's crew | Wintering at Lowmarch's upper inn: Teague (Force; Bronze by a registry he stopped reporting to; about forty; a wrist that clicks), the tall woman (spear), the broad man (crossbow; a limp), the young one, and the older woman with the cloth bag (a healer of no Path). **All but Teague stay unnamed.** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:20:| Vastin | Inside the Compact, writing nothing (one window in Book 7). **Age not stated in this edition** (OWNER #17). "Forty years" is his own rounding. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:27:- His ten fragments, their costs and deployment notes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:29:- Four sites lie on one bearing. The Ring, Stair and Hall were entered. The fourth was paced from outside: 400 m radius, numbered registry iron a pace apart, at least forty stakes counted, not entered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:31:- The Compact surveys quiet ground, from the kit's ledger: a radius line, an index of forty-one kinds, the stroke-and-bar mark, and "third site confirmed on bearing".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:41:**Karis knows:** the 52 sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall); that the carvings *command* rather than describe (from their shape, at the Hall); the strata; [UNBOUND] as a stratum limit (Book 7 Ch15, used once); the sub-layer; that the kit's index is an index, not what it indexes. She has read of the old scholars' provision in a register "years ago".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:50:- **Pike's sheet:** nine completed lines under the five names. The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. **Eleventh** on the wall; Teague's four are top. The season line is blank, left so on purpose. The axe-head hold's fence slip (forty, HOLD, the five names) is taken, unpaid until it is done.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:51:- **The kit** (Compact, registry-stamped, recovered at the Stair): the case; the pacing cord, knotted at the fives (twenty strides to a cord, end-loops worn shiny); stake number thirty-two (point bright); the mallet; the field ledger (the surveyor's square hand; the radius line; the one designation entry for the Stair, in an unreadable index; "third site confirmed on bearing"). No pen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:57:### Fragments and progression (ten confirmed; the still place uncounted)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:19:### Entry (Book 7 close; source Ch1 opens on the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:21:- **When/where:** Lowmarch, the day after the ferry's last run. First snow lies on the town and the river is skinning with ice. The book's calendar runs by the Line's count, day 131 to day 308.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:32:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:33:- **The reveal is delivered once, in the record's voice:** the leaf in the Deepstacks. "The Architect" is the record's title; the name is scraped away; it was about four hundred years ago; the purpose was "that the un-bound should not come again". The chronicle's "went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" is **marked, not read**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:37:- **Vastin** is on the stick until day 30 of Oryn's month ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:38:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say."). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:42:- **Body ledger at close:** Brom's forearm is bound (bolt, pass) and he has a week of colours. Karis's left hand is bound and will scar ("It'll leave a line"). The broad man's leg is knit and his shoulder bound. Teague's arm faces a splint warning. Vastin is on day 29 of 30. Cael's ribs "will carry. They'll hurt."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:51:1. **KEEP — The winter frame (S1, 131st–264th).** The ferry has gone and the count has stopped moving. Inventory: nineteen, ten fragments, 96 marks. The winter is priced: "Meadow rate is four a month for a crew that's on my sheet" / "Eleventh", twenty paid in front, leaving 76. Teague's chin-lift across the yard; the season line left blank on purpose.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:52:2. **KEEP — Pike's winter board and the fence (140th).** Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:53:3. **KEEP — The river is a road (161st); the kit on the table.** The cord is knotted at the fives, the stake is number thirty-two, plus the mallet and the field ledger with the radius line. The Stair's designation sits in an unreadable index above the stopped line "third site confirmed on bearing". Karis learns the kit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:54:4. **KEEP — The anomaly (168th).** The yard paces forty-two strides for everyone and "forty-one and a piece" for Cael, three times. The Ternhall edge reads a hair short in his hand and Hesk's edge a hair long. Karis's ruler sentence is said twice: a rule, then not a rule. Logged: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:56:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her spring's first stops. Nobody asked her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:58:8. **KEEP — The ferry (277th).** Vastin arrives alone, in a brown coat, with an ash stick, a pack mended with cord and a bad knee. "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." Pike prices him: "What'd he do?" → "Then he's nothing yet." He pays a copper and a half for bread. Teague reads his hands a step longer than a crew looks. Lira's face for men in grey doesn't fit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:60:10. **KEEP — The handover (277th evening)**, in Vastin's stated order. First, the records: a courier's flat of six years of survey abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), six rows, "More than four", and the completion report as the last sheet. Second, the page: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". Third, the technician's sheet: the deep-layer line and the brush bar; Karis copies it and writes "not read". Seln goes still and does not say the sum. Vastin's vertigo; Karis owns the response. Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:61:11. **KEEP — The slip (278th).** Clearance at the cut below the shoulder hold, twenty. "Ours" twice. Pike writes a sixth line for the healer. Vastin is not on the sheet and walks at the back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:62:12. **KEEP — The cut (279th).** Iron Wall is first shown: a plane across the road, rooted, and therefore loud. Brom fights silent with a rock. Lira works the scree. Cael bursts away, then goes still on the scree; the pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap. Seln in the heap. Five dead and three into the sink. Costs: Brom's foot; **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson: "The wall held the line. And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." / "You do now." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:63:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (his Kindling day; five years and a hundred-some days; "six" is the office's rounding), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:65:15. **KEEP — The last day of the road (281st).** Lira makes the same discipline of the crown, unasked. The reading inward, a fourth and fifth time: "a cord on a stone"; the instrument is wrong for a stillness. Vastin sits; "You were the instrument. I was the error." Vastin's confession, narrowed (ruling 18): "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." Cael gives him the instrument's nothing. It is not friendship; it is ground. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:71:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:81:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:83:33. **KEEP — The crest (303rd).** The watch-post: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, a two-timber barricade, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" "Nobody declares. Nobody dies … Noted?" / Teague's first **"Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:84:34. **KEEP — The Span (304th).** First exchange: the watch's declaration is unanswered; Brom takes bolts on Iron. Teague goes through the middle (the barricade a body's length back) → **Force acquired** at a stride. Recoil: wrist, then elbow. The watch reforms. **Width:** "Nothing was gained inside" is entered first. "By count": five over stake thirty-four (Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin), four on the shelf. They walk to the pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east, unpursued. The win sentence (§10). The broad man goes over the sink's edge in the fourth second; Teague does not turn. Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers' nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's bill. **The Span** at noon: an arch on two piers over the sink, carvings on the piers' inner faces, the bearing "Through". Nothing happens on the crown. The thirteenth listens. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall woman's first words to the six in a year.** The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:87:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:89:39. **KEEP — The centre (307th dusk).** 506 strides. Rune turned on the floor at a hundred strides gives the same reading. The eyes are paid. **No edge, no seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. The third sentence goes unsaid. Oryn reads him at the line ("May I?"): "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He told nobody. The count. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:117:1. **Cael's working inventory in winter** (≈6,000; first third). Through private practice in the ferryman's shed and the frozen meadow, the reader learns all ten fragments as costs and limits. Wind's burst and its locked landing beat. Pressure's narrow channel. The Iron read as "the workhorse". Compression's frame. Ember, never used. Shadow's idle draw and the seal's logic. Storm asleep. Anchor used both ways. Blade, short and sharp. Tide "ask first", which he cannot practise on anyone and does not read on himself (Oryn said stop). **Invent no new numeric ceilings.** Costs are qualitative unless canon gives a number.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:119:3. **Vastin learning the crew's doctrine and "to be nobody"** (≈5,000, distributed). Day one of the border road is a silent-movement drill: walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless meant to be loud. Then the cut's lesson, the spring's "Draft nothing", the yard door's "Be nobody", his week of moving toward the lamp and stopping (four times, then two), and the first order he takes and keeps (Millrace).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:120:4. **The Deepstacks decipherment** (≈8,000). The chamber days 285–292 are put on the page, including the undramatized 288th–289th. Cleon's method (bones before words), the board's numerals, Karis's letters coming one at a time from the three floors, and the lamp's discipline. Karis refuses to guess. **The leaf must not become readable on the page before the seventh day** (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:127:- **The winter months (131st–264th)** (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The board in winter. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:129:- **Treswick's days** (≈8,000). The outer district as a mechanism: brokers' tally boards, the smith's two forges, the ring road at night. The undramatized chamber days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:130:- **The 294th: the list of parts** (≈2,000). Copying all day, Cleon's finger on the last line, and his correction "Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:136:### D. Supporting-cast arcs — ten people, many small beats each (≈40,000 including cutaways)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:144:| **Oryn** | The route; to be nobody's recruit | Releases the arm only when Lira lifts the sling herself. Comes to Lowmarch unasked. Sets the station term in the log. Routes north. Rejoins as a stop. Asks every time. Walks on east at the cairn. Will not hear the leaf at her table. Turns north "the day I have to". | 11 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:155:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:159:Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:167:| 1 | The Count Stopped Moving | 1–6 | 30,000 | S1 (whole) | Put the winter on the page; teach the ten fragments, the kit and the anomaly hard; pay the Thornwater promise; end on six and west. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:171:| 5 | No Authority | 27–33 | 35,000 | S10, S11, S12 | The archive's first days; Vastin unlearning his name; Cleon's bones; Brom offered the life; the alley and the eleventh. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:194:| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
