editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25:- **The road east (295th–297th; ~5,000).** On the bridge he counts five piers, and does not look at the crown. The spring, with the wind in their faces this time. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited:** "Here." Vastin puts his weight on the knee with the stick off the ground, once. "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted" (Cael's). The feeling of being *known* is entered under each date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30:- **The deep reading (~3,000).** "May I?" / "Yes." It is the long one. Her current goes round the place. **The twelfth turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** It is not named, and he keeps the check out of his wrist and the change out of his face. The eyes pay in the dark. **Oryn's finding, verbatim.** He withholds his own and enters his reasons in order. Lira offers the leaf. "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf …" / "Then it's not mine … Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33:**Physical challenge:** the road and the cut walked again on a bad knee. Force seen. As a learning encounter, the two crews work together in the Lowmarch meadow, **silent movement and march order only. They do not drill under a wall** (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:27:- **The spring (280th).** Three readers. The instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size; "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin has three reflexes: a directive, a classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. **Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael.** Cael does the sum: his Kindling day, five years and a hundred-some days back. He does not write it, and puts the sheet back. Then: "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone. **Close, verbatim:** Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:32:**Cutaway (~1,800):** Seln at the spring. He does the sum and decides to set the sheet in front of Cael without a word. He weighs what it costs to give a thing without saying it. He does not theorize about the deep layer. **The cache stays unopened and undecided.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:46:The drill's details and Vastin's mistakes in it. Exactly how the pack moves on ice. How long the scouting takes. The spring's light and wind. The order in which the three readers find things. How Oryn prices each of them, and the fork's last fire. Whether Vastin's three reflexes come in one scene or across the halt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:33:- **Burial and the plain's edge (306th).** Teague's crew builds the cairn in their own order. The six carry at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." **"That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now."** No term tonight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:38:- **The line again.** Oryn: "May I?" / "Yes." "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He tells nobody what the centre felt like and gives them the count instead. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:39:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "Next spring … My crew comes." Oryn: "The day I have to." … "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say." "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:28:  - The Hall's marsh, where Cael read himself twice in the autumn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:31:- **The crest.** The watch-post: hut, fire, kit under a hide, two timbers, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." Seln: "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" Cael draws it. "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / Teague's **first "Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:48:**Cutaways (~5,500):** Seln, ~1,800, on the crest at night or along the perimeter before dawn. He reads the iron and the watch. The cache stays unopened. Teague, ~1,700, in the watch's hut after the fall. He counts his crew; the broad man's leg; the young one asleep. **Nothing of the mechanism. Not the young one's name.** Karis, ~2,000, the night after the lamps finding. She holds the refusal in her own head, knows the six-word sentence exists, and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:12:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §1 Entry; §2 items 1–7; §3 A (shale-back fence, ice road, silent yard), B 1–2 and B 7, C (winter); §5 (the Karis and Teague cutaways); §6; §7.1–7.2; §10 Tier B and the Ch1/Thornwater lines in Tier C; §13.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:21:Put the winter on the page and teach hard. This is the first third, so the formula wants progression vocabulary at its densest here. The reader should finish the movement knowing all ten fragments as costs and limits, and the kit as a tool. They should know that instruments read wrong in one pair of hands, and why Karis cannot let go of the index. The movement ends with six at a table and a word nobody has said yet: west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:24:- **The winter priced** (133rd): Pike's four a month; "Eleventh"; seventy-six left. Then the board in winter: a roof, a well-house, a fence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:25:- **The fence at the axe-head hold** (~140th, ~3,000 for the set piece). This is two days out on the winter road. A shale-back herd shelters on the fence line's slope and must be moved without stampeding, with no Path that matters. Lira is benched in her sling and reads the herd for them. Brom reads the line of posts like a wall. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. The factor pays forty at the gate and asks no name: 116, and the tenth line, PAID.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:27:- **The silent yard** (two or three bouts across the winter, ~1,500 each). Teague's crew and the five spar in the frozen meadow with steel and bodies, and no Paths. Cael loses to the tall woman's spear reach, then makes a visible correction. She never says a word to any of the five. Lira coaches from the bench, one-armed. The rival clock appears on the page. Teague is the better field captain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:30:- **Karis's case grows in pieces** through the winter. She says the full sentence about west on the 263rd. The thaw comes, and the Thornwater road opens on the 264th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:35:**Cutaways (~4,500):** Karis, ~2,500, on a winter night with the index: her want, and her refusal to theorize about the cord. Teague, ~2,000, at the upper inn: the young one asks to learn; the wrist; he cannot read the sheet and does not need to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:49:How many chapters the winter takes, and which log entries become scenes. The shape of the herd problem and the ice rescue. The content of the silent-yard bouts and who wins each. The texture of the inns, the board room, the ferryman's shed, and the long dark. Letters gone west, with answers pending (none arrive in this movement). Humour: Pike's ledger speech; Brom's "It's a boot"; the mule's shed fee "he has not asked for and will".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:17:It is the 270th day at Lowmarch. There are six now, with Oryn's spring stop at Pike's plank. Lira has two arms she does not quite trust, and Brom's shoulder is still bound and unread. The ferryman says the ice will go in a week, and has said so for a week. Karis's case is made and no one has answered it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:24:- **The week before the ferry** (270th–276th). Tents return to the meadow. Oryn's patients come to the plank, seen from outside. Teague's crew gets ready for spring.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:28:- **The long table** (midday). The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, verbatim; these are their first words to each other. Vastin says the short thing: he resigned or walked out. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence ("Under every station on the continent. I said so at a table in the autumn"). Vastin's new fact: "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail ends at Treswick. Vastin then has nothing to do. Lira asks "Why us." Oryn notices the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that crosses the Line, and the Stair's rim "is not mine". Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only, "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks. **Close (verbatim).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen (turned nineteen in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **No birthday this book.** Ribs quiet since the marsh, healed under a healer's two days that became four. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. The ten fragments are at rest. The still place is untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:98:- Teague's spring term.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:25:- **Teague's crew** winters at Lowmarch: four plus the healer of no Path. His term: "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:38:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say."). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:39:- **Teague** turns west with three practitioners and the healer of no Path. **The young one is dead**, buried under stone at the pass's east mouth. His name was said once by the broad man and is never written. Teague carries Cael's letter to Hesk. "Next spring. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:51:1. **KEEP — The winter frame (S1, 131st–264th).** The ferry has gone and the count has stopped moving. Inventory: nineteen, ten fragments, 96 marks. The winter is priced: "Meadow rate is four a month for a crew that's on my sheet" / "Eleventh", twenty paid in front, leaving 76. Teague's chin-lift across the yard; the season line left blank on purpose.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:52:2. **KEEP — Pike's winter board and the fence (140th).** Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:56:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her spring's first stops. Nobody asked her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:63:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (his Kindling day; five years and a hundred-some days; "six" is the office's rounding), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:81:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:83:33. **KEEP — The crest (303rd).** The watch-post: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, a two-timber barricade, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one winter." Teague: "Drawn?" "Nobody declares. Nobody dies … Noted?" / Teague's first **"Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall woman's first words to the six in a year.** The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall woman reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:87:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:89:39. **KEEP — The centre (307th dusk).** 506 strides. Rune turned on the floor at a hundred strides gives the same reading. The eyes are paid. **No edge, no seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. The third sentence goes unsaid. Oryn reads him at the line ("May I?"): "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He told nobody. The count. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:96:Nothing below may change an end state, move a death, add an acquisition, or disclose a reserved truth early (§11). Every new episode must fit the sequence locks in §13. Word figures are planning estimates, not quotas.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:105:| **The pass** (rig; seven volleys; the death) | S21, ~3,800 | 5,500 | This is the book's costliest fight. The terrain causes two beats (the fall, the swept scree). The young one's death must be prepared and not gratuitous. Force's first use is paid in the ribs. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:106:| **NEW — The shale-back herd at the axe-head fence** (winter) | summarized as "we walked the fence" | 3,000 | A winter set piece needing no Path: a herd of armoured grazers sheltering on the fence line's slope must be moved without stampeding them ("lethal on a slope when herded wrong"). It teaches the Iron read on frozen ground, Lira benched by her sling, Seln's posts, and Brom reading a line. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:108:| **NEW — The silent yard** (winter learning bouts with Teague's crew) | absent | 3 bouts × ~1,500 = 4,500 | No Paths, steel and bodies only, in the frozen meadow. Cael loses to the tall woman's spear reach (she never speaks), then corrects. One-armed Lira coaches from the bench. The rival clock appears on the page. This must not touch the sequence locks in §13 (no wall drill; Seln teaches nobody). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:113:| **Lesser exchanges given their beats** | — | ~4,500 | The alley's aftermath; the Span's broad-man fall; the ridge recovery of the mule; the court's pacing as a physical task. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:117:1. **Cael's working inventory in winter** (≈6,000; first third). Through private practice in the ferryman's shed and the frozen meadow, the reader learns all ten fragments as costs and limits. Wind's burst and its locked landing beat. Pressure's narrow channel. The Iron read as "the workhorse". Compression's frame. Ember, never used. Shadow's idle draw and the seal's logic. Storm asleep. Anchor used both ways. Blade, short and sharp. Tide "ask first", which he cannot practise on anyone and does not read on himself (Oryn said stop). **Invent no new numeric ceilings.** Costs are qualitative unless canon gives a number.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:119:3. **Vastin learning the crew's doctrine and "to be nobody"** (≈5,000, distributed). Day one of the border road is a silent-movement drill: walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless meant to be loud. Then the cut's lesson, the spring's "Draft nothing", the yard door's "Be nobody", his week of moving toward the lamp and stopping (four times, then two), and the first order he takes and keeps (Millrace).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:127:- **The winter months (131st–264th)** (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The board in winter. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:128:- **The week before the ferry (270th–276th)** (≈4,000). Tents return to the meadow. Teague's crew prepares for spring. Oryn's first Lowmarch stop: patients at the plank, seen from the outside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:132:- **The leg (299th–303rd)** (≈9,000). The Stair's bowl rim, where Karis checks a number for an hour. The cairn: Oryn chooses east. The Hall's marsh, where Cael read himself twice in the autumn. Two dry camps. Two crews learning each other. The crest at dusk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:142:| **Karis** | To be right and believed, with a primary source | Learns the kit. Makes the case for west. Owns the response to Vastin's flat. Reads the leaf once and asks that nobody say it back. Keeps two pages at a spring, a hole and a fire. Sits with Vastin after the pass. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Teague** | To be at the front of the thing; to keep his people | Holds the spring term. Names the contract's terms. Goes through the middle. Does not turn when the broad man falls. Does not put his three across the court's line. Carries the letter. | 7 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:148:| **Pike** | An honest ledger | Prices the winter. Prices Vastin at nothing yet. Leaves the season line blank, then dates it. | 4 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:167:| 1 | The Count Stopped Moving | 1–6 | 30,000 | S1 (whole) | Put the winter on the page; teach the ten fragments, the kit and the anomaly hard; pay the Thornwater promise; end on six and west. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:179:**Quiet-movement statement:** Movement 4 is the book's one deliberately partial-quiet movement. Its tension is legal and bodily: a [SHATTERED] body enters a Compact city whose top holds a station. Its learning encounter is the reading inward (the instrument fails). Its physical load is labour: four hands, three tiers, two gates, a bad knee and a box. It may carry one small physical beat of the author's choosing, but it does not need a fight. Every other movement has at least one fight, set piece or learning bout.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Karis** | ≈7,500 (3) | M1: a winter night with the kit's index (her want; the cord reads wrong only for him, and she refuses a theory). M5: decipherment (board numerals; the first letters). M8: the night after the lamps finding (the refusal held in her own head). | The sheets; strata; the index (as unreadable until the 298th); the leaf (after the 293rd); the lamps finding. | The Rune finding (nobody knows it). The integration of Rune before Cael tells Lira. **Drawing the line**: her interior names that the sentence exists and refuses it. The deep-layer date as Cael's Kindling. The leaf's content before it is read aloud. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:195:| **Teague** | ≈7,000 (3) | M1: the upper inn in winter, watching the five; the young one asking to learn; the wrist. M7: deciding the contract's terms; the meadow. M8: the watch's hut after the Span, counting. | His crew; Force and its line; the contract; the board; that he does not read. | The integration mechanism, including any suspicion that the boy took his Force. **The young one's name.** Any reading or writing (he does not read). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:197:**No cutaway may disclose a reserved truth (§11) or any sequence lock (§13).** A cutaway may show a person's private want and an independent decision. It must not reveal a fact the plot later "discovers" in Cael's POV.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:201:## 6. Calendar spine (continuity; the author may move scenes within a day)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:206:| 133 | Winter priced (76) |
