editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:31:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:34:- **Five on the bearing (122–123):** the ridge with white lines in its folds; Seln's "Nothing" every hour; **"I love this country."** at noon, with the dread in the same coat. **The fourth site from the crest at dusk:** "Larger." A valley head; a standing grey shape taller than a man, neither ring nor stair, that the dusk keeps. Lira's *gone* at about a hundred and ninety paces, not forty. Twenty cords paced along the line from outside, half the bend: four hundred. **The cordon**, iron a pace apart, numbered thirty-four with the stroke and the bar, both ways (forty counted, and more). "That's not a survey. That's a cordon…" **The council: five voices and one silence** (protected). Nobody crosses. Camp on the crest; the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:40:- **The fourth site is not entered and not named.** Its effect on a Path is unknown. There is no watch-post and no undated "years" on the cordon. Its silhouette stays ambiguous (Book 8 makes it an arched span on piers).
