editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:265:- Vell (Ch9): *Filed with your record. It reads: left in good standing, undefeated on paper. I've kept this ledger forty years and never had a line like it. The session still stands. The road still runs through Ardenmere. — V.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:268:- Cael to Vell (Ch24): *Vell. There's a second ledger on the continent with my name in it, kept by a one-armed man in a town on no map, and this week he stopped numbering me. He said his book was wrong about us by being too small. You said once that somebody should have a record that doesn't answer to the Compact. There are two now. The session still stands. — C.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "One thousand three hundred and seventy-four yards, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:308:- Ch11: Seln: "The road's cut." … "The grass. Where the cord went." — Oryn: "Move," … "I can't fix this here. Move." … "She keeps it." — **The order:** "A mend that deep holds nothing for a season. Nothing. That arm is not to hold. It's not to strike. It's not to catch. Not a rope, not a knife, not a fall, not a friend. Not until I say. And I'll say at first snow, near enough, if it's let alone." … "One arm. From here to the snow." — "The ankle's a tape and a season. I've told you that before." — Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes," Cael said. / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:317:- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:320:- Ch23: Karis: "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." — "That's a healer's sentence," Oryn said … "I know whose it is," — Brom, Lira, Oryn at the first halt: "Twice," / "Twice," / "And not three," — Oryn at the fork: "I'm three weeks late there…" … "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days. I'm going back to being the route." … "Find me at Thornwater," … "Bring the map," — Karis: "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see." — Seln: "That's not a survey. That's a cordon. They've been here more than once." — Lira: "Twice the size. Is it twice the *anything else*?" — Cael: "Not without her. Not without knowing what a circle twice the size does to the four of you. And not without the map finished." / "It's finished," Karis said. "It's a line." / "Then it's a line that points somewhere. We go home and find out where."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:334:| The Quieting's source (Architect reset; B10–11) | Observable mechanics only: perfect circle, about 220 yards [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2], sharp line, identical failure, fused floors, carvings, fauna denning | Spread; growth; any city; any change in a site's size |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:336:| The instruments reading wrong in his hands (B8 plant → B11) | Nothing | Any cord, stake or straightedge reading off in Cael's hand. **In Ch24 both edges touch for him as for Karis.** Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:337:| The Compact's six-year suppression / directive (B8) | Fieldwork only: stakes (31; 32 twice, one re-surveyed with the stroke-and-bar; 33; the 34 cordon), the maps' blanks, the kit and its ledger, a completion report going west | Policy, files, offices, the word "suppress," any date on the cordon, the stroke-and-bar or the index decoded |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:338:| The fourth site (B8's Sunken Span) | Paced from outside: about 190 paces to the line, twenty cords, half the bend, about 440 yards [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]; a standing grey shape taller than a man, neither ring nor stair; the cordon | Entering it; naming it; its effect on Arbiters; a watch-post; a sink, a bridge or piers seen clearly |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:352:- **C3 · Karis's measurements.** Ch23: "I've paced two and cord-measured the third." The Stair's perimeter was never paced on the page (Ch18: "I'll pace it in the morning", and the morning was the trap). At the Hall she stood "with the cord in her hand and not laid" (Ch21). **Recommend:** stage the Stair pacing on the morning of day 115 under Teague's rim watch, and the Hall's cord laid during the two marsh days (119–120). Ch23's sentence and the bible's "same radius at the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall" then become true on the page.

