editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:3:This is the book's entry state, taken from canon (the Book 7 close in `universe/STATE_LEDGER.md`, Book 7 Ch23–24, and the source edition's Ch1 inventory). After each movement is drafted, append one section built from the surviving prose, not from the plan. Where the prose and the plan differ, record the prose and note the difference. The binding end state is `BOOK_MAP.md` §1. The sequence locks are §13, and the owner-facing conflicts are §12. If the edition's own Book 7 rewrite moves any seam fact below, reconcile this section before Movement 1 is compiled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen (turned nineteen in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **No birthday this book.** Ribs quiet since the marsh, healed under a healer's two days that became four. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. The ten fragments are at rest. The still place is untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:41:**Karis knows:** the 52 sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall); that the carvings *command* rather than describe (from their shape, at the Hall); the strata; [UNBOUND] as a stratum limit (Book 7 Ch15, used once); the sub-layer; that the kit's index is an index, not what it indexes. She has read of the old scholars' provision in a register "years ago".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:47:### Resources
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:59:| # | Fragment | Source | Standing notes at entry |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:105:*(Append one section per movement below, from the drafted prose: bodies, injuries, knowledge, resources and cash, fragments, relationships, open threads, and any plan/prose difference.)*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:7:Source of record for events: `books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-01.md` … `chapter-24.md` (102,657 words by `tools/formula_metrics.py`). The prose governs where it differs from `CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md`. The architecture's header and plant text still carry superseded items (a twentieth birthday in Ch14, "the Still Court", a "sixth" site); the rulings in `v3-runs/book-08/DECISIONS-B7-RECONCILIATION.md` (rows 1–25) and the final review `v3-runs/book-08/reports/book-scope-review-r3.md` govern. Canon: `universe/` (bible, rules, ledger), `series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md` (Book 8 entry and neighbours), `craft/NAME_REGISTRY.md`, `craft/VOICE_CHARTER.md` (Reader Standard), `editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md`. Book 7 Ch23–24 were read for the entry seam. Book 8 is the last written book; the seam forward is the series bible's Book 9 entry (§15).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:19:### Entry (Book 7 close; source Ch1 opens on the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:30:### Ending (source Ch24, dawn of the 308th; must hand off to Book 9)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:32:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:47:## 2. The spine — every major source event, in order (all KEEP)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:49:Dates are the Line's count. A source chapter is shown as (S*n*).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:71:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:100:| Fight / set piece | Source | Edition allowance | Why |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:127:- **The winter months (131st–264th)** (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The board in winter. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:142:| **Karis** | To be right and believed, with a primary source | Learns the kit. Makes the case for west. Owns the response to Vastin's flat. Reads the leaf once and asks that nobody say it back. Keeps two pages at a spring, a hole and a fire. Sits with Vastin after the pass. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:165:| # | Title | Chapters | Words | Source retold | Reason (one line) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:185:**Cael ≈87% (≈261,000 words).** It is close third, tinted by his habit of cataloguing. The source's long, accumulating "catalogue" sentence is his signature, and the edition keeps the habit while breaking the chains (§7.4).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:267:| **The instruments** (Book 11 plant) | M1 (cord; edges: a hair); M3 (the row counts a sheet short); M6 (the station's light for a count of one); M8 (the row short at the Span); M9 (a stride short; a hair and a half, two) | Deniable each time | Trend up; unsourced; "no line drawn" |
