editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:306:The source's signature is the accumulating catalogue sentence, chained with "and … and … because …". That produces both the 19% of sentences over forty words and the paragraphs of fifty-plus words, while very short beats pull the median and the Flesch score up. **For this edition:**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:334:- **The chronicle's hole stays a hole.** "Marked." There is no gloss, guess or second source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:343:Tier A is quoted in the canon files (bible, ledger, series entry) or is a system notice. Tier B is wording from earlier books that this book quotes; it is binding from its own book. Tier C is fixed by the source architecture as closers or fixed lines; keep it verbatim, because Book 9's planning will read the source. Straight quotes and em dashes as in the source; italics are not wording.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:376:### Tier B — earlier books' wording quoted here (binding from source)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:378:- Karis (B7 Ch20): "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (in Ch1's form; S5, S15 and S20 use "A measurement is a fact about a ruler. Not about the hand that held it.")
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:379:- Karis (B7 Ch24): "Someone made this pattern." Karis (B7 Ch23): "Three points make a line. Four make an argument."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:380:- Oryn (B7 Ch23): "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." Oryn's letter (B7 Ch24): "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O." / "Six, by letter."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:381:- Hesk's straightedge note (B7 Ch24): "Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:382:- Teague (B7 Ch24): "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." Pike (B7 Ch24): "I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:384:- The still-place inventory (B7 Ch24): "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues." Oryn: "stop touching it". The Tide rule: "ask first, every time".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:387:### Tier C — source-fixed lines and closers (keep verbatim)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:389:- **Ch1 closing log (270th):** "The ferry runs when the ice goes. Karis has a bearing, an index she can't read, and a language she can't read, and she says the answers are in a border archive nobody's opened since before the Compact. I've spent five years staying out of registries because a registry is where they file you. She wants me to walk into the oldest one on the continent. The kit reads everyone but me. So does the world, mostly. Nineteen. Ice goes next week. West, and inside, for the first time since the academy above Ostrand — which is a sentence I did not think I'd write again." And the 168th: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:425:| The Quieting's source, spread and reset | 10–11 | Every site is old and stable. **No first-tier site is produced** (the box stays unfilled). No maker's present will, no purpose beyond the leaf's, no spread, no reset. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:426:| The Fractured Path is primordial | 13 | Never *primordial / before / source* about Cael. Interior read as *structure*, felt not explained. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:434:## 12. Canon conflicts found in the source (with the edition's working ruling)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:436:- **C1 — Vastin's age.** The source states "Fifty-three, or near it" (S2), "at fifty-one" (S7) and "fifty-three-year-old" (S10). The universe ledger records 53. OWNER-DECISIONS #8/#17 default: *age never stated; career "forty years"*. **Edition: no stated age.** "Forty years" is kept as his own rounding (ruling 20). *Owner ruling welcome; it does not block.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:439:- **C4 — The grandmother.** The universe ledger lists "Hesk's grandmother" as the owner of the straightedge saying. Book 7 Ch24's note ("Your grandmother said…") and S17/S24 make her **Cael's** grandmother, Hesk's late wife. **Edition follows the prose.** The ledger line is a slip.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:441:- **C6 — Architecture residue.** The architecture's header, plant ledger and checkpoint still say Cael turns twenty in Ch14, the terminus is "the Still Court", and there is a "sixth" site. **Superseded** by rulings 12 and 13 and by the closed prose: nineteen throughout, "the court", the fifth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:442:- **C7 — Reveal locus.** CANON_RULES says "ancient records in edge-territory ruins"; the bible says a "pre-Compact archive at a border city". The source stages both: the leaf is in the Treswick archive and its key is the ruins' carvings. **Flag for the bible pass.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:446:- **C11 — "Tell Lira's family I said so"** (S24 letter to Hesk, kept by the final review). The referent is unclear: no Book 8 scene sets up Hesk carrying word to Lira's family. **Kept verbatim as source-fixed; owner to confirm intent** (it may be a callback the edition's earlier books should plant).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:448:- **C13 — Reader Standard repairs already made in the source.** Seln does not lie at the yard door (ruling 25). Consent is asked before every reading (S18 montage and Cael, S22, S24). **The edition carries both and adds no exception.** The source has no profanity and no gore to remove.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:449:- **C14 — Calendar of the leg.** STATE_RUNNING's first Ch19 note put the cairn on the 301st; the closed prose puts it on the 300th, with the crest on the 303rd. **Edition follows the prose** (§6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:450:- **C15 — Rhythm (not canon).** The source runs a 21.3-word sentence mean, 19% of sentences at forty words or more, and a paragraph median of 51. The edition re-builds the sentences (§7.4), and Tier C wording stays verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:495:- The baseline metrics in §7.4 were measured with `editions/monroe-1.3/tools/formula_metrics.py` over the 24 source chapters.

