editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:29:- **The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. Cael gives **Lira the page to read first**; nobody explains it to her. "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom prices it. Seln will keep the cache "a while longer". Karis says two pages, then sleeps on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, taken on his feet and not catalogued, verbatim. "I want to stand in the middle of it." Cleon leaves: "Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22:The leg goes on the page as the place where two crews learn each other, and where the young one becomes someone a reader will grieve. Then the fourth site: a watch-post, a barricade, a captain's line, and a width that wins because the people inside the line have stood there before, with nothing gained by it. The thirteenth arrives. The next night every finding goes onto one blanket, the lamps finding is said aloud and filed on its own page, and a marshal finds a crack he does not pry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:27:- **The spring (280th).** Three readers. The instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size; "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin has three reflexes: a directive, a classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. **Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael.** Cael does the sum: his Kindling day, five years and a hundred-some days back. He does not write it, and puts the sheet back. Then: "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone. **Close, verbatim:** Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:40:- Vastin's age is not stated. Oryn does not read Cael; "the one thing I'm walking up that road owing".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:21:This is the archive's first week. Karis has found the room she has wanted all her life. A marshal learns his name is a blade with no handle. A craftsman shows how he reads a made thing's bones. Brom is offered the life his family wanted and picks up a box. Seln looks at the door his old trade would have used and decides nothing. Then the faction reaches inside the walls. A man with nothing behind him holds a line for people the Compact would restrict, and Cael comes away with the eleventh. We cross the first third into the middle, and progression language surfaces at the turning points: Rune explained, Iron Wall paid, the notice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The Deepstacks (284th).** The galleries, the shelving, the smell of a place where nothing has been decided. Cleon reads to the end of his page first. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." Cleon: "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael finds himself, for the first time, unfiled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:49:- Vastin does not know the mechanism and his age is not stated. "Forty years" is his rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:41:- Vastin's age is not stated. The clerk is not named and asks nothing.
