211:- **The plank (flag):** twelve feet of tarred ship's oak on two posts under the lower inn's eave; slips on bark, hide, a shingle or paper, each on one tack, with a small picture beside the words for people without letters; Pike's horn ink-pot set in a bored hole; his flat river stone for the page; an iron box bolted under the plank for the hirers' coin.
214:- **HOLD (flag):** a captain asks Pike to keep a slip by until he is back; "Anybody can ask. I've said yes to one."
219:- **Shadow's source habit (flag):** Seln learned it on a stair as a boy; "a year to do on purpose and three more to stop doing by accident"; it came at dusk. Two drifts in Cael (day 5, four strides; day 24, one stride), logged as rent.
220:- **Roles (all unnamed):** the courier (about fifty, a split lip long healed, a hat cut away on the right, a hatchet in a saddle loop); the three carts' people, who are one group throughout: the old carter with two mules, who takes the shade of the ash; the boy of about fifteen; the hide-woman, who is also the wash's hirer; the ferryman and his boy; the standing-money boy; the smith; the landing broker and his clerk; the old man of the north-water steading, his white dog, his goat; the Thornwater carter (short, thick, twenty-two years on his road); the steading's woman (broad, a grey braid); the bowman; the north-road woman captain (a red cloth round her hair; two men and a girl); the eleven-bale captain (a new coat).
221:- **The road's craft:** two cairns set to mark a slanting ford; stock watered below the crossing; the stone rings on halting-grounds are for chocks, not fires; a carter's axles kept in mutton fat, trace chains bound in sacking, heel-plates cut off.
222:- **Fauna:** red-barked conifers with flat paired needles (Karis will not name them; "red not-pine" is entered as Lira's); a broad pale tree with silver-backed leaves; grey long-legged deer with white rumps that are not afraid of people.
223:- **The wash (flag):** three hours out on the east road; twelve feet deep and thirty across; a ramp on each side; a thorn stump on the eastern lip.
228:- **Teague, as seen (flag):** forty or so, middle height, heavy in the forearm, cropped hair grey over the ears; a black leather band laced on the right wrist; a hand-axe in his belt; a coat mended by somebody else. His week on the cold road is salt on mules to the top holds before frost shuts the pass, along two miles of ledge; he has done it nine times. He thinks only "the spear", "the bow" (a bad leg), "the boy". One other crew on the sheet could clear the ford and is up the north road.
230:### State at movement end (author; updated after repair r1)
232:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the gate-to-stone distance is a hundred and ten YARDS (Cael paced it at a yard to the stride; Seln's hundred and four longer paces agree with it); the animal "tracked the buckle" and no sense is named anywhere; Pike's Thornwater line is printed once, in chapter 6, and its saying in chapter 7 is narration; the twelve-second doorway hold is recalled at Thornwater's ladder, not in the day-18 inventory. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures.*
234:**Calendar.** The evening of the **forty-ninth day past the Line**, in the lower inn at Lowmarch. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page; "Fifth-day" appears twice (ch4, ch5) as the academy's own word. Days on the page: 2 (night), 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10–12, 14, 15–21 (drills; the catalogue on the 18th), 22–24, 30 (Seln, the cold road), 33, 41, 42, 43, 44–46, 48, 49. Weather: warm, dusty, long light; the roads "dry right through" from about day 46; one storm over the eastern ridge on day 33. The next movement opens on day 51.
238:**Cael.** Eighteen, said to Pike on day 9. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly** (*Still open. Still real. Patience.*, written on day 18). **Deployment since the Line: none.** No injury; the forearm is "sound again" by day 5 and is not mentioned afterward. Idle states: Shadow sealed, costing from waking, drifting at dusk (two drifts, logged as rent); Anchor asking at every sill, gate, rim and rail; Blade asking *Edge?* and taking names; Storm heavy; Wind leaning his feet. He has not read the Iron read once. The log has an entry for most days, each ending on the deployment line.
244:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Uninjured. Sets no points on a road. Holds: the field archive; a leaf headed *stillhound*, underlined once, with five counts and *110 yards* (*gate to stone; C.'s count, paced at a yard to the stride; not taped*); the entry of her own not-asking (day 22); the five column heads with *Outcome* underlined twice; Pike's copied line; **the carter's map**. She has asked nobody what the animal is waiting for.
246:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze, said once at a fire. Uninjured. Has not lifted his Path since the crossroads fire. Has walked the first hours of eight roads, five out of Lowmarch and three out of Thornwater; on day 49 he says, in one sentence, that he has walked the first part of all five out of Lowmarch. Has the prints and the forty-five-yard line by the white stone in his head, a hundred and ten yards from the gate (a hundred and four of his own paces), and has told nobody. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
252:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. Pike has not asked what Cael is, and has said that he never asked. Three people have called him paper and been told yes. The party knows the word *stillhound* and nothing of what it hunts by, or by what sense it followed a buckle; it has Cael's five counts, Seln's unshared reading of the ground, and the country's rule without its reason. **Nobody has heard the words "quiet ground".** Teague has read the five and found Seln on his second pass; he cannot tell what Cael is. Cael has read Teague. They have not spoken.
254:**Open threads.** What a road hears. What the grey thing waits for. Why a hundred and ten. Why it will not cross wet gravel. The forty-mark slip, held a week for a crew that leaves at dawn, on a stretch that took two carts last month. Lira with no ladder. Brom's first earned coin. Karis's price for not asking. Seln's eight roads, waiting to bear on a day. The second question nobody put to the steading's woman. Vell, of whom Pike has never heard. The hook and the bar.
265:- **Local relationship continuity:** the hide-woman is the same person who gave the cake and hired the wash recovery; Thornwater's woman, bowman and carter have already seen the crew hold; the carter gave Karis his twenty-two-year map in exchange for Brom's wheel repair (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:3-5`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:285-353`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:13-55,187-211`).
277:- **Deployment since the Line: ONE** — a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53. None before; none after. Shadow is unused by Cael and stays sealed. Seln's use of his OWN native Shadow Path under water at the ford is not Cael's deployment and stands (it tested the water clause).
280:- **Quiet ground** remains three sentences from the carter's wife, spoken as one speech. Nobody asks. The bend on the carter's map two days east of Thornwater, round bare hide, is the only geography; Movement 4 inherits it.
282:- **Bodies:** Cael bitten through the calf ("the calf in elevens"); Karis's hand cannot hold a pencil; Lira's ankle splinted, then walking; Brom's shoulder in a sling. Exact states are in the author's state section below, as corrected after repair.
283:- **All new canon KEEP** (plan audit §6): the lip stones; "the third" as a man of the hold; the flint fire on the road lit on the strength of the finding, with the hold unchanged; the well's bad air; Pike pricing Brom's part at "a fifth of forty"; the closing bare tack.
287:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial (pass; one register priority), cold read (three clarity items), source-distance (6 tracked passages, no dense scene), plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — twelve applied by the coordinator). Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows below when the recheck returns.
291:- **The ford's ground (flag):** a river some fifty yards wide over a single ledge of grey rock, **the sill**, ten feet broad, with two wheel-grooves and green slime; shin-deep fast water over it; a slow glide above; below, a **lip**, and pools that fall away over a man's head. A gravel **bar** in mid-river, thirty yards by eight, lying with the stream, its blunt head at the sill and its tail running down between the two pools to a point. A near (Thornwater-side) and a far channel, twenty yards each; a near and a far beach; a cut bank a man's height above the near beach.
295:- **The finding (flag), as dictated by Karis and written in Cael's log:** the stillhound hunts Path discharge; it hears and sees a little, and uses both only to keep its place and to try a quiet body with its teeth; water masks it at both ends (a wading hound goes to where the declaration was when it left dry ground; a Path held under water for an hour and a quarter drew nothing at eleven feet); there is no leader, only whichever moves first; they learn. Not accounted for: 110 yards; dusk.
305:- **Lowmarch:** undirected eastbound mail stops at Pike's plank; he gives out each piece twice and reads letters at dusk to people who have no letters; a spike under the plank holds finished slips; he rewrites the whole wall on fresh sized sailcloth when the order changes; a crew entered as *the shingle pair* is thirteenth from day 60.
307:- **The well (flag):** at the south road's fork, half a day out on level ground; a dry-stone curb, a windlass; paid from the standing-money. It went sour at the thaw; a carter's boy was drawn up asleep. Foul air lay fifteen feet deep on the water at thirty feet. Pike's line: *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.*
308:- **Roles (all unnamed):** the hold's boy on the leaning mule; the man with the bound arm; the clouded-eyed east carter, his wife, and the small boy on her foot-board; the shingle pair; the southbound carter whose son went down the well.
311:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: the steading's woman's last word is about HEALERS ("Healer would've had it straight in an hour." / "There isn't one." / "There's not. They stop inside, where the tiers are."), Lira says "There isn't one", and nobody asks the woman about ranks; the thought that ranks stop there too is Lira's own, said at the fire. Cael learns of the bite when his left foot drags and he sits down in the river (Seln sees it first; no blood in the water). The finding begins as a line of Cael's own, which Karis strikes and replaces by dictation. The day-57 log gives no "earned" figure; Thornwater's yard has no stride count; Hesk's letter is known by its fold. Owner flag 5 above is superseded by the coordinator's amendment. Word counts, metrics, line numbers and the protected-units table elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the repaired chapter 13 also carries the protected three-speech unit at lines 35–41.*
317:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53, in front of the hold's bowman). Shadow unused; it lifted at dusk through the wait at the ford and again on the walk down the bar and was refused. Ember offered a point in the hound's mouth over Karis and was refused. The Iron read stays shut. Left calf bitten through on day 53: a leg on level ground, nine strides uphill. He has not asked Seln for his report, has not answered Lira's question, has not answered Hesk's letter, and has stopped counting Lira's runs. He knows that he had a grandmother who crossed the Line once on a trade run; no name, no line of descent.
323:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. One point lit and put out at the ford; none since. Two pink lines across each palm; a pencil again on day 68. Holds: the hypothesis leaf; the finding (in Cael's log, by her dictation, and in the field archive in Lira's hand); a leaf headed *This side.*; the carter's map; and, in the middle box, the carter's wife's three sentences with *everybody knows* underlined twice. She has asked nobody what quiet ground is, Seln included.
325:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze (not said in public). Lifted his Path once, under water, on day 53; killed the seventh hound. Unmarked. Walked the south road to the well first, alone, and said nothing. Has said aloud that he keeps waiting to be asked for his report. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut**; it spent the evening of day 53 in Thornwater's loft.
329:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Six lines** under the five names: the protected ford line (said on day 60) and *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.* (day 64). **Twelfth of thirteen; Teague eleven up.** The ford slip is with the finished slips, struck with one line through Teague's name and five strokes beneath, and Thornwater's mark at the foot. Fourteen slips on the plank on day 60; a bare tack set by the left-hand post on the evening of day 69 for a hold's slip expected from the north-west.
331:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. The hold's bowman saw one Wind burst and took it for a Path. The party now holds the stillhound finding in five sentences. **Quiet ground is three sentences from a carter's wife**; nobody has asked Pike or anyone. Thornwater knows the five as the crew that came up from its ford. The party knows from the hold that one healer walks a route and is not due, and that healers otherwise "stop inside, where the tiers are". Teague has read the struck slip and the line and said nothing; no meeting.
