     1	# BOOK MAP — The Fractured Path, Book 8: Before the Paths (Monroe Jackson 1.3 edition)
     2	
     3	Seat: O'Connor 1.3.0 (`oconnor`), foundation Monroe Jackson 1.3.0. Public byline: Monroe Jackson.
     4	Planning seat model: Claude Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`), as reported by the runtime. Requested manuscript author: Opus.
     5	Plan date: 2026-10-01. Status: PLAN ONLY. No manuscript prose exists for this edition.
     6	
     7	Source of record for events: `books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-01.md` … `chapter-24.md` (102,657 words by `tools/formula_metrics.py`). The prose governs where it differs from `CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md`. The architecture's header and plant text still carry superseded items (a twentieth birthday in Ch14, "the Still Court", a "sixth" site); the rulings in `v3-runs/book-08/DECISIONS-B7-RECONCILIATION.md` (rows 1–25) and the final review `v3-runs/book-08/reports/book-scope-review-r3.md` govern. Canon: `universe/` (bible, rules, ledger), `series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md` (Book 8 entry and neighbours), `craft/NAME_REGISTRY.md`, `craft/VOICE_CHARTER.md` (Reader Standard), `editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md`. Book 7 Ch23–24 were read for the entry seam. Book 8 is the last written book; the seam forward is the series bible's Book 9 entry (§15).
     8	
     9	**Shape at a glance:** 9 movements · 60 chapters · 300,000 words · average 5,000 words per chapter · largest movement 36,000 words.
    10	
    11	**Book promise (series bible):** make the reader feel the weight of history: the present is built on something that was deliberately buried.
    12	**Internal arc:** *the system was built to exclude me* → *the system was built specifically to prevent me* → at the oldest centre, *he fit*. The third sentence past those two stays unwritten.
    13	**The title:** "Before the Paths" names two things. It is the era before the classification existed, when the un-bound walked in the land. It is also the book's argument: everything in Valdris was laid on top of a buried thing by someone who wanted it to stay buried. The book's image is a Compact registry built on the roof of a pre-Compact quarry it has never read.
    14	
    15	---
    16	
    17	## 1. Entry state and ending state (binding)
    18	
    19	### Entry (Book 7 close; source Ch1 opens on the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line)
    20	
    21	- **When/where:** Lowmarch, the day after the ferry's last run. First snow lies on the town and the river is skinning with ice. The book's calendar runs by the Line's count, day 131 to day 308.
    22	- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
    23	- **The five at Lowmarch:** Lira (Wind, Iron R1 formal) has her left forearm slung and load-restricted by Oryn's order since the Ring, and the right ankle taped and unmended. She carries Oryn's crossbow. Brom (Iron Skin, Copper formal) has his right shoulder mended twice ("not three times this season"), then bound, and carries it still and forward. Karis (Ember, unranked by choice) holds 52 copied sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall), the kit's field ledger, the carter's map with four circles and the bearing, and the Ternhall straightedge. Seln (Shadow, Bronze) has the cache on his back, unopened. Cael has Hesk's brass straightedge.
    24	- **Oryn:** at Thornwater on her route. "Six, by letter." Lira's arm waits on her word, and she owes Cael a full reading.
    25	- **Teague's crew** winters at Lowmarch: four plus the healer of no Path. His term: "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted."
    26	- **The Quieting:** four sites lie on one bearing. The Ring, the Stair and the Hall were entered. The fourth was paced from outside at 400 m radius and is cordoned in numbered registry iron, not entered. "Someone made this pattern" was asked once and not answered.
    27	- **The Compact:** it has reached across the Line twice, on paper (the completion report) and in person (the Stair's rim). It knows quiet ground exists and which crew walks out of it declaring. It does **not** know what works inside. The asset-restriction is pending. **Vastin is still inside**, writing nothing, with one window in Book 7.
    28	- **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn. Nobody else knows: not Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon.
    29	
    30	### Ending (source Ch24, dawn of the 308th; must hand off to Book 9)
    31	
    32	- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
    33	- **The reveal is delivered once, in the record's voice:** the leaf in the Deepstacks. "The Architect" is the record's title; the name is scraped away; it was about four hundred years ago; the purpose was "that the un-bound should not come again". The chronicle's "went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" is **marked, not read**.
    34	- **Five sites lie on one bearing, ages ascending east.** The court is the fifth and the oldest, 1,012 m across, and the end of the line. It is **unnamed** ("the court", lowercase). The taxonomy is decoded: a stroke alone, a stroke and bar, a stroke and two bars.
    35	- **Karis's lamps finding** is stated and filed unexplained, on a page separate from the leaf, with no line drawn between them.
    36	- **The crack:** a directive and a filed objection under two seals that Vastin could name and does not.
    37	- **Vastin** is on the stick until day 30 of Oryn's month ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
    38	- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "Spring. Bring the map. Lie still when I say."). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
    39	- **Teague** turns west with three practitioners and the healer of no Path. **The young one is dead**, buried under stone at the pass's east mouth. His name was said once by the broad man and is never written. Teague carries Cael's letter to Hesk. "Next spring. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes."
    40	- **The faceless faction** has reached three times (the alley, the Span's watch, the pass) and broken each time. It is unnamed, unlocated and faceless.
    41	- **Count at the rim:** "Six. Six and no mule." That is Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Vastin. The word is "West."
    42	- **Body ledger at close:** Brom's forearm is bound (bolt, pass) and he has a week of colours. Karis's left hand is bound and will scar ("It'll leave a line"). The broad man's leg is knit and his shoulder bound. Teague's arm faces a splint warning. Vastin is on day 29 of 30. Cael's ribs "will carry. They'll hurt."
    43	- **Cleon** stays under Treswick with the leaf and the board: "Work. Not a finding."
    44	
    45	---
    46	
    47	## 2. The spine — every major source event, in order (all KEEP)
    48	
