   340	
   341	## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; canon quotes or calls back these, or Book 9 inherits them)
   342	
   343	Tier A is quoted in the canon files (bible, ledger, series entry) or is a system notice. Tier B is wording from earlier books that this book quotes; it is binding from its own book. Tier C is fixed by the source architecture as closers or fixed lines; keep it verbatim, because Book 9's planning will read the source. Straight quotes and em dashes as in the source; italics are not wording.
   344	
   345	### Tier A — canon-quoted and system text
   346	
   347	1. **The leaf (S15):** "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again."
   348	2. **The chronicle (S15):** "— and of him it is said that he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" [a thumb's width of hole]. Karis: "Marked." Cleon: "Marked."
