     6	- Word budget: 38,000
     7	- Days: 116–131 past the Line
     8	- Owner names: canon only. Teague's crew (including the older healer of no Path), the hide carter, the ferryman and his boy, the old woman at Thornwater, the carters at the fire and the inn's keeper stay unnamed. **The fourth site stays unnamed.**
     9	- POV: Cael ≈29,900. **Teague cutaway ≈1,700** (days 117–120: following the crew's trail three days along a bearing he does not understand, the healer brought because a shoulder was mended once; sitting down beside the boy; the column). **Karis cutaway ≈2,000** (days 119–120 at the far fire: three copies, the ledger, the edge laid and moved; it ends exactly on the pencil stopping; no who or why). **Seln cutaway ≈1,600** (days 124–128, the road home: the ledger in his coat; giving it to Karis and not asking for it back). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,800** (day 122 to about 128: the gap north-west, four days, three weeks late; Thornwater; the old woman's knee; writing the letter, ending on its four lines).
    10	- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈55 per 10k (the still place, the inventory, the map). ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for all six, plus Teague, Pike and Teague's healer.
    11	
    12	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — still-place continuity (Sol plan audit, Movement 6), binding.]** ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.
    13	
    14	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator O3]
