editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:36:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The cold-term fence** given over ("Ours.") [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]. Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "After the thaw." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:45:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:46:- **Ninety-six in hand. Nine lines. Eleventh.** The kit is on the table. Fifty-two sheets.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:55:Book 8 Ch1: Lowmarch with the ice coming and the ferry's ropes taken in. Ninety-six in hand. A kit on a table. A map with a line going off its edge. A healer at Thornwater with a route and an arm to release. A captain's after-thaw term. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] A fourth circle twice the size behind a fence of iron. And a question asked once at a table that nobody answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Seln cutaway ≈2,200** (night of day 112, after the council: the two slips laid side by side in his head; twelve years carrying the case for people he cannot see [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B6]; why he wants a face; he may not open the case or decode anything). **Teague cutaway ≈2,400** (days 113–115: at Millrace, the five not back; the walk south to look; the rim's ground read in lantern light, the crossbows, "declaring"; holding the rim at dawn without being asked; no crew names).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:14:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — still-place continuity (Sol plan audit, Movement 6), binding.]** ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20:> Movement 7’s packet already carries the day-111 start, Oryn gone, mule with the crew, Lira two weeks into the order, and the report west (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20`). It must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:22:> - **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment thirteen; Shadow still only once; the eleven Wind leans are practice; the tenth has read only himself, once; two further self-readings on different days and the whole telling to Oryn remain owed; he may read nobody merely to test the ability; Oryn’s answer and remaining price stay withheld (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `chapter-40.md:189–211,319–385`; `chapter-44.md:167–209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:23:> - **Bodies:** Lira’s left arm remains slung and may hold nothing until first snow, although all eight marks have taken; right tibia may run; right ankle remains taped/unmended and her left arm cannot span the bow. Brom’s hand is whole. Karis’s voice is whole but she must not lecture for a week. Cael’s calf is closed and forearm yellow-marked. Seln is unhurt (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:103–121,129–201`; `chapter-43.md:125–159`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:24:> - **Equipment and money:** 102 marks in hand; three boxes and Oryn’s mule; Seln’s shut case; Oryn’s empty pannier left on the saddle while she carries the other and the spare rope; the yard crossbow, belt hook and five bolts travel with Brom; the ring sheets, bark slips, four chips, calfskin rings and charcoal round remain in Karis’s boxes (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`; `chapter-41.md:3–39`; `chapter-42.md:205–277`; `chapter-43.md:171–215`; `chapter-44.md:209–245`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:27:> - **Open accounts:** Pike has eight completed lines but the crew has not heard the eighth read at the board; the Fallow hundred remains in Pike’s box, the ferryman’s rope and two HOLD slips remain unresolved, Hesk’s parcel has not arrived, three letters are unanswered, and seven hounds remain untracked (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–263,383`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:173–179`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28:> - **Oryn:** day 112 closes just short of the mill; she is sixteen late out of Thornwater and seventeen late at Oxhollow, has left the mule, and has not forgiven Cael or received the self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:223–301`). Her exact location on day 113 is Millrace under M7, subject to the protected north conflict (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator O3]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:36:First light on the 111th at Thornwater: Oryn gone north, her mule with the crew. Lira is two weeks into the season's order. A completion report sits on a desk west of the Line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43:- **Pike says the Fallow line before the door is shut;** it costs a line (eleventh; "Teague's ten up"). Then what the wall cannot say: thirty years, forty-odd crews, nobody over a line and back, "Six in and six out, and the sixth a healer." **The room updates** without a word (the hide-woman, the crew of three gone grey, the carter from the first week, the boy). **Teague stands** when they come in and sits at "eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:45:- **The council, the second honest collision:** Lira for walking away (the fence at forty and the walk at fifty, and pace the third circle on their own time); Brom ("Three hundred's a number a man doesn't reach for." — his father and the horse); Karis ("I would go alone."); **Seln: "Take it… People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face."** [OWNER-pending #50] Cael's sentence to the whole table (protected), then why: the assumption is wrong and cannot be known to be wrong. **Brom quotes Rooke**, the first person he has ever quoted: "Doors open both ways… I don't like it. I'm in." Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away." The log (EXC-B7-002). Pike marks HOLD unasked and says it to the room. **Teague at the door** (protected): "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted.", the first *Noted* to anyone above them on the wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:48:- **The Stair from the ridge at dusk:** a bowl wider and shallower than the Ring's; a bare floor with no ring; a square hole with three lit steps and then dark. The line at forty paces ("Two hundred. I'll pace it in the morning."). **Two stakes numbered thirty-two**, one under five cold terms of scale [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] and one under one or two, with the **stroke and the bar**: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed." Camp at the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:49:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty-five yards** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Once Cael is within ten feet of the knot, Anchor perception finds it; he then makes the separate purposeful unbinding, without assigning that action a measured reach, rate or price [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:50:- **Out at dark:** "There. Back… The clock started again." The bolt-head cut and the shaft drawn; an hour on Brom; a quarter on Lira ("It held a stair…"). His bill: the suite spent on a week's rest. **Seln breaks a stock across the stone**: "No faces." The log (protected). **Teague's crew at full dark** (protected exchange); he does not ask how.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:51:- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:59:- Oryn joins as a stop on her route, never as "sixth," never "join." The Stair slip's three hundred is taken and never paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:68:Day 115, at the stone in full sun. The kit is on Brom's good shoulder and his bad one is mended once. Lira's arm is closed again with the sling higher. The ledger is in Seln's coat; twenty-nine sheets and forty-one kinds. A brass edge lies on a map. A dead man's last word was *bearing*. "We're going to go look."

