118:## 41. Book 5 tournament calendar re-dated after M6 (coordinator default, 2026-10-05)
119:M6 defers the exhibition ring (west-tower notice, T5); the ring is complete at dawn T11. New spine: Shield captain T11; duelist and Vastin's seat T14 (chair held thirteen days, replacing "nine"); rest day/birthday T15; team trial T16; filing T19; convening T20; third place T21; finals T24; closing T26. Recorded in book-05 BOOK_MAP §6 [M6-redated] and the M7 packet. Owner may restore a tighter span; the birthday date itself stays pending under #35.
123:- **Season-blind B6 (#19 vs #35/#37 O1):** #19's restructure keeps its SHAPE (one academic year; served on the eighth day; the cache and Vastin before the midyear recess; the ruling in the year's last month; the Line crossed after the year's close) but carries NO season or month names — "the year's first weeks", "the cold term", "the midyear recess", "the year's last month", weather words for texture. "December" is struck. Owner may restore seasons when the series calendar is ruled (#35, #36.4).
126:- All other A/B/C items applied as the audit proposes; §D (PENDING B5 M9, incl. A11 "a stamp renewed four times") re-run the day B5 M9 closes.
132:The Compact's formal challenge (B6 ch5, Tier B first page) addressed "the enrollee of record, Cael, unclassified". Book 5 makes registry usage explicit: official instruments use *Caelen Hesk-ward* (B5 ch2:5; ch5:87, Karis: the tournament roster's line was "the first time any official paper has ever called him what we call him"). Default in force: amend the one noun phrase of Tier B text to *the enrollee of record, Caelen Hesk-ward, unclassified,* — the rest of the first page unchanged (Tier B permits recomposition where a word is wrong; this is a canon correction, recorded here). M2's house answer addresses the same name. Owner may restore "Cael".
144:The protected Tier B minute reads "*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*" In this edition Gault is the evaluator of record and the Archmarshal's office is the certifying office that declined. **Ruling: the protected line stays verbatim and is read as the form's own mislabel** — an old column heading with no place for the right office — which the scene already dramatizes (four pens stop; Gault "had declined nothing"). One plain sentence was added outside the protected line so a young reader is told so directly: "The refusal was the Archmarshal's; the form's old column had only Gault's title to put it under." Owner may instead release the protected line and have it name the certifying office.
148:- **Season-blind and feet/yards, continued into Book 7** (as #37 O1 and #42 did for Books 5 and 6). Named seasons and metric units are replaced, minimally, INCLUDING inside Book 7's protected lines (for example "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." becomes "After the thaw. …"; "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." becomes the same distance in yards). Generic "season" and "month" stay. Every changed protected line is listed, old and new, in `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md`; the owner may restore any or all when the series calendar is ruled.
155:Seven protected lines say variants of "mine didn't", "my Path", "mine has been asleep since I was fourteen", "dark since fourteen", "every Path … his had not". Edition canon (Book 6): Cael's own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and the Arbiter went dark; he has no Path. At a Quiet line the others' live Arbiters stop, his is dark before and after, and his fragments still answer. **Default until ruled: the protected lines stay verbatim**, the surrounding plan and prose state the canon, and the lines read as Cael's own shorthand. Options: (1) release only the conflicting clauses for a minimal canon repair; (2) release the affected log entries for clean re-composition; (3) keep as is (the default).
160:The protected line gives Seln six years; edition Book 6 has him carry the case twelve years (fifteen in service). **Default until ruled: the line stays verbatim** and the plan stops calling the case a six-year matter. Options: (1) "Twelve years I've wanted a face."; (2) "All these years I've wanted a face."; (3) keep six and name a separate event six years back that began the wish.

